(window.AeroSenseTranslations ||= []).push({"A fly-brain route from curiosity to understanding.":"循著果蠅腦的路徑，從好奇走向理解。","Why education belongs in the project":"為什麼教育是專案的一部分","A fact can be understood.":"知識可以被理解。","A decision has to be practised.":"決策則需要練習。","Education is a right, and a way for people to take part in decisions that affect them. Article 26 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights and SDG 4 give that commitment a public foundation; Target 4.7 connects learning to sustainable development. For AeroSense, it means making the science accessible enough to question, use and eventually build on.":"教育是一項權利，也讓人們能參與影響自己的決策。《世界人權宣言》第 26 條與 SDG 4，為這份承諾提供公共基礎；目標 4.7 則將學習與永續發展相連。對 AeroSense 而言，這代表要讓科學容易理解，使人能夠提問、運用，並最終在其基礎上繼續建構。","Our initial survey changed the question we wanted to ask. Explaining that mold can be dangerous was too broad. Our working summary pointed instead to decisions people make about heat, smell and visible spoilage. We therefore built opportunities to choose an answer, see why it matters and try a new situation. The team now reports 107 responses; item-level counts still need verification, so this page does not turn the early summary into population percentages.":"初期問卷改變了我們想問的問題。只解釋黴菌可能有危險，範圍太廣；工作摘要反而指向人們對加熱、氣味與可見腐敗所做的決策。因此，我們設計讓人選擇答案、理解其重要性，再嘗試新情境的機會。團隊目前回報 107 份回覆，但逐題人數仍待核實，因此本頁不會把早期摘要轉換成人口比例。","Active participation gave us a useful starting point. Freeman and colleagues' synthesis of 225 undergraduate STEM studies found an average 0.47-standard-deviation improvement in examination performance with active learning. Wouters and colleagues found benefits of serious games for learning and retention, with no clear overall motivation advantage. Those results justify testing an approach; they do not establish that our own games work.":"主動參與提供了有用的起點。Freeman 與同事綜整 225 項大學 STEM 研究，發現主動學習平均使考試表現提升 0.47 個標準差。Wouters 與同事發現嚴肅遊戲有助於學習與保留，但整體動機優勢並不明確。這些結果支持我們測試此方法，卻不能證明我們自己的遊戲有效。","We also wanted a conversation about synthetic biology itself. What does it mean to put a fruit-fly odor receptor into cultured HEK293 cells? What can a fluorescent response tell us? Who should act on a screening result? Each activity below gives a different audience a way into those questions.":"我們也希望開啟關於合成生物學本身的對話。把果蠅氣味受體放進培養的 HEK293 細胞，代表什麼？螢光反應能告訴我們什麼？誰應該依據篩檢結果採取行動？下方每項活動，都為不同觀眾提供進入這些問題的方式。","Our education journey · a fly-brain map":"我們的教育旅程 · 果蠅腦地圖","The route borrows three landmarks from the fly olfactory system: sensory input reaches the antennal lobe, projection neurons carry information toward the mushroom-body calyx, and mushroom-body output pathways link learned information to behaviour. We use that route as an educational metaphor for first contact, deeper understanding and sharing what has been learned. The biological circuit has feedback and parallel pathways; the map is a reading guide.":"這條路線借用果蠅嗅覺系統的三個地標：感覺輸入到達觸角葉，投射神經元將資訊送往蘑菇體萼部，蘑菇體輸出路徑則將學到的資訊連結至行為。我們用這條路徑作為初次接觸、深入理解與分享所學的教育比喻。生物迴路存在回饋與平行路徑；這張地圖是閱讀指南。","01 · Antennal lobe":"01 · 觸角葉","First contact":"初次接觸","Survey, three games and social media: find the question that gets someone to stop and think.":"問卷、三款遊戲與社群媒體：找到讓人停下來思考的問題。","Enter the input stage ↗":"進入輸入階段 ↗","02 · Mushroom-body calyx":"02 · 蘑菇體萼部","Build understanding":"建立理解","Connect biology, measurement and interpretation through a curriculum and guided learning.":"透過課程與引導式學習，連結生物學、量測與解讀。","Enter the learning stage ↗":"進入學習階段 ↗","03 · Mushroom-body output":"03 · 蘑菇體輸出","Take it into a room":"把知識帶進新的場合","Explain the work to new audiences, exchange questions and leave resources others can reuse.":"向新觀眾解釋研究、交流問題，並留下可供他人重用的資源。","Enter the exchange stage ↗":"進入交流階段 ↗","Region 01 · Antennal lobe / input":"區域 01 · 觸角葉／輸入","Olfactory signals first converge in the antennal lobe. Our first educational layer also brings many starting points together: a survey surfaces existing beliefs, a game makes a pattern tangible, and a social post reaches a person who was not looking for a science lesson.":"嗅覺訊號首先在觸角葉匯聚。我們的第一層教育也匯集多種起點：問卷呈現既有觀念，遊戲讓模式變得具體，社群貼文則接觸原本沒有在找科學課程的人。","The survey gave us a question to work on.":"問卷給了我們一個可以著手的問題。","The diagnostic asked about food storage, visible mold, heating and the reliability of smell. We use it to identify concepts for discussion, rather than to label an audience as uninformed. Its educational role is to connect a familiar household decision to the limits of a signal: seeing or smelling one feature cannot answer every food-safety question.":"這份初步診斷詢問食品儲存、可見黴菌、加熱，以及氣味是否可靠。我們用它找出值得討論的概念，而不是把觀眾標籤為缺乏知識。它的教育角色，是將熟悉的家庭決策連結至訊號的限制：看見或聞到某一項特徵，無法回答所有食品安全問題。","Our response was a short decision exercise followed by an explanation and a chance to reconsider. The questions below are for the visitor; choices stay in this browser tab and do not add respondents to our study.":"我們的回應是簡短的決策練習，接著提供解釋與重新思考的機會。下方問題供訪客練習；選擇只留在此瀏覽器分頁，不會新增至研究受訪者名單。","28 responses informed the redesign; 107 is a later collection total.":"28 份回覆提供重新設計的依據；107 是後期蒐集總數。","The team’s engineering narrative cites the early questionnaire record on":"團隊的工程敘述引用了早期問卷記錄，日期為","23 August 2026":"2026 年 8 月 23 日",". Most respondents already rejected the three claims. We therefore replaced broad awareness messaging with decisions about heat, visible mold and sensory evidence. The date and item counts for the later 107-response collection have not been supplied; no result below is attributed to that larger denominator.":"。多數填答者原本就否定這三項說法，因此我們將廣泛的意識宣導，改為對加熱、可見黴菌與感官證據的決策練習。後期 107 份回覆的蒐集日期與逐題人數尚未提供；下列結果皆不歸屬於這個較大的分母。","Early diagnostic summary — n = 28; source-reported aggregate counts":"早期診斷摘要——n = 28；來源回報的彙整人數","Claim respondents correctly rejected":"填答者正確否定的說法","Correct rejection count":"正確否定人數","Share of early sample":"占早期樣本比例","Cutting off visible mold makes the rest safe":"切掉可見黴菌，剩下部分就安全","Heating or roasting fully eliminates mycotoxins":"加熱或烘烤會完全消除真菌毒素","Normal appearance and smell establish no risk":"外觀與氣味正常，就能確定沒有風險","Download the aggregate table (CSV)":"下載彙整表格（CSV）",". Percentages are calculated from the reported integers. The raw questionnaire export, coding file and missing-response breakdown are not available. This non-random, consumer-skewed sample informs what to teach; it is not a population estimate or a pre/post evaluation.":"。百分比由回報的整數人數計算。原始問卷匯出檔、編碼檔與缺答分布皆無法取得。這個非隨機且偏向消費者的樣本，用來決定教什麼；不是人口估計，也不是前後測評估。","Diagnosis":"診斷","This is not a data-collection form and not part of our research sample. Choices stay in this browser tab. They are not stored, sent, logged, or added to n = 107.":"這不是資料蒐集表單，也不屬於我們的研究樣本。選擇只留在此瀏覽器分頁，不會儲存、傳送、記錄或加進 n = 107。","Claim 1":"說法 1","Cutting off the visible mold makes the rest safe to eat.":"切掉看得見的黴菌後，剩下的部分就可以安全食用。","Do you agree or disagree with this statement?":"你同意還是不同意這個說法？","Agree":"同意","Disagree":"不同意","Scientific interpretation":"科學解讀","Disagree. Removing a visible colony does not automatically make the rest of a food safe. In some firm foods, public guidance allows cutting away a margin; in soft, moist, or porous foods, mycelium and some mycotoxins can extend beyond what you see. “Always safe” is the over-claim.":"不同意。去除可見菌落，不會自動讓食品剩餘部分變安全。某些質地堅實的食品，公共指引允許連同周圍一段範圍切除；但在柔軟、潮濕或多孔的食品中，菌絲與部分真菌毒素可能延伸至肉眼看不見的地方。「一律安全」是過度主張。","Claim 2":"說法 2","Heating or roasting fully eliminates mycotoxins.":"加熱或烘烤會完全消除真菌毒素。","Disagree. Heat may inactivate molds without eliminating heat-stable mycotoxins. Killing or reducing the organism is not the same as removing the metabolite. “Fully eliminates” is not a safe general rule for ordinary cooking.":"不同意。加熱可能使黴菌失活，卻未必消除耐熱的真菌毒素。殺死或減少生物，不等於移除其代謝物。對一般烹調而言，「完全消除」不是可放心通用的規則。","Claim 3":"說法 3","If it looks and smells normal, it’s not risky.":"只要外觀與氣味正常，就沒有風險。","Disagree. Appearance and smell cannot establish mycotoxin status. Absence of an off-odor does not prove absence of toxin; presence of mold does not by itself quantify a toxin. Sensory inspection is not an assay.":"不同意。外觀與氣味無法確立真菌毒素狀態。沒有異味，不能證明沒有毒素；有黴菌，也無法單憑這點定量毒素。感官檢查不是檢驗。","Survey data status":"問卷資料狀態","The early record contains 28 responses and three aggregate item counts. A later total of 107 is team reported; its item-level analysis has not been supplied.":"早期記錄包含 28 份回覆與三題彙整人數。後期總數 107 是團隊回報，尚未提供逐題分析。","Limitation":"限制","An initial diagnostic, not a population estimate.":"這是初步診斷，不是人口估計。","The design decision rests on the early n = 28 summary, not the later n = 107 total. Neither stage supports population prevalence or learning gain.":"設計決策依據的是早期 n = 28 摘要，而不是後期 n = 107 總數。兩個階段都不支持推論人口盛行比例或學習增益。","Non-random sample. People were not drawn with a sampling frame that supports inference beyond this group.":"非隨機樣本。參與者並非透過可支持推論至此群體之外的抽樣架構選出。","We used this to choose":"我們用這份資料選擇","what to teach":"要教什麼",". We do not use it to estimate how common these beliefs are in the public.":"，不以此估計這些觀念在大眾中有多普遍。","Scientific readings":"科學解讀","The interactive choices require JavaScript. The 107-response survey's item-level results are pending verification.":"互動選項需要 JavaScript。107 份問卷的逐題結果尚待核實。","Removing visible mold does not automatically make every food safe.":"去除可見黴菌，不會自動讓每一種食品都變安全。","Ordinary cooking does not guarantee removal of all mycotoxins.":"一般烹調不能保證移除所有真菌毒素。","Appearance and smell do not establish toxin status.":"外觀與氣味無法確立毒素狀態。","Online games · Odor Pixel Suite":"線上遊戲 · 氣味像素遊戲套組","A smell is a pattern across channels. That sentence is easier to understand after a pattern has fooled you. Our three browser games turn recognition, navigation and mixture decoding into decisions a player can try. They are simplified teaching models, with formal learning evaluation still pending.":"氣味是跨通道的模式。當你曾被一組模式誤導過，這句話就更容易理解。我們的三款瀏覽器遊戲，將辨識、導航與混合物解碼轉成玩家能嘗試的決策。它們是簡化教學模型，正式學習評估仍待進行。","01 · Recognise":"01 · 辨識","Odor Pixel Lab":"氣味像素實驗室","Match an odor to a pattern of receptor-like signals, including patterns with noise. The question is how identity survives imperfect measurements.":"將氣味對應至類受體訊號模式，也包含有雜訊的模式。問題在於：量測不完美時，氣味身分如何仍可辨識？","Play the pattern game ↗":"玩模式遊戲 ↗","02 · Navigate":"02 · 導航","Odor Maze":"氣味迷宮","(Scentbound Labyrinth)":"（Scentbound Labyrinth）","Explore a maze and use scent information unlocked along the route. The activity makes a signal useful through the choice it helps a player make.":"探索迷宮，使用沿途解鎖的氣味資訊。這項活動透過訊號幫助玩家做出的選擇，展現訊號的用途。","Enter the maze ↗":"進入迷宮 ↗","03 · Decode":"03 · 解碼","Odor Fingerprint Mixer":"氣味指紋混合器","Explore overlapping patterns from odor mixtures. A mixed fingerprint is an interpretation problem, which connects the activity to AeroSense's decoding layer.":"探索氣味混合物形成的重疊模式。混合指紋是一個解讀問題，也讓活動連結到 AeroSense 的解碼層。","Explore the mixer ↗":"探索混合器 ↗","Open the complete bilingual suite":"開啟完整雙語遊戲套組",". Educators can use the":"。教育工作者可以使用","optional study protocol":"選用研究流程","to pair responses. Casual visitors can start playing immediately.":"來配對回覆。一般訪客則可直接開始遊玩。","Three formats for a scrolling audience.":"為滑動瀏覽的觀眾設計三種形式。","The survey and the games ask people to seek us out. Instagram lets us introduce the same ideas in a feed they already use. We separated that work into technical carousels, sustainability questions and short explanations, each with a different job.":"問卷與遊戲需要人們主動找到我們。Instagram 則讓我們在他們原本就使用的動態消息中介紹相同概念。我們將這項工作分成技術輪播圖、永續提問與簡短解說，各自承擔不同任務。","From a fly nose to an edge device":"從果蠅的鼻子，到邊緣裝置","The first carousel asks, “What if we put a fruit fly's nose inside a human cell?” It explains the intended chain from odor recognition through calcium to a fluorescent reporter. The two published teaching graphics below make the receptor and reporter visible. Fluorescence in our experimental system still needs to be characterised against controls; brightness alone is not a calibrated odor-concentration scale.":"第一組輪播圖問：「如果把果蠅的鼻子放進人類細胞呢？」內容說明從氣味辨識、鈣離子到螢光報導蛋白的預定鏈結。下方兩張已發布的教學圖，讓受體與報導蛋白變得可見。我們實驗系統中的螢光仍需與對照比較分析；單看亮度，不是經校正的氣味濃度尺度。","Parts Design · an entry point into the living-sensor idea.":"元件設計 · 進入活體感測器概念的起點。","Parts Design · connecting molecular components to the intended signal.":"元件設計 · 將分子元件連結至預期訊號。","The two published Parts Design graphics are the current technical series.":"目前的技術系列，是兩張已發布的元件設計圖。","covers the decoding and reader carousels and short science videos.":"涵蓋解碼與讀取器輪播圖，以及科學短影片。","Sustainability Pop Quiz":"永續小測驗","Four question-and-answer cards connect a design choice with an SDG. Open a card below to see the intended connection.":"四張問答卡片，將設計選擇連結至 SDG。開啟下方卡片，查看預期的連結。","Earlier warning of disease in a fruit shipment?":"更早對水果貨運中的病害提出警訊？","SDG 2 · Zero Hunger.":"SDG 2 · 消除飢餓。","The intended benefit is more time to decide what to do with a batch. Detection lead time and avoided loss still need measurement.":"預期效益是增加決定如何處理批次的時間。偵測提前量與避免的損失仍需量測。","A biological sensor with a custom optical reader?":"生物感測器搭配客製化光學讀取器？","SDG 9 · Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure.":"SDG 9 · 產業、創新與基礎設施。","Building local research and engineering capability. The integrated platform's performance and power are validation questions.":"建立在地研究與工程能力。整合平台的效能與功耗仍是待驗證問題。","A cartridge designed for repeated readings?":"為重複讀取而設計的匣體？","SDG 12 · Responsible Consumption and Production.":"SDG 12 · 責任消費與生產。","Reuse is a design aim. Lifetime tests and a life-cycle comparison must establish any reduction in waste.":"重用是一項設計目標。是否減少廢棄物，必須透過壽命測試與生命週期比較確認。","Design choices changed by people outside the lab?":"實驗室以外的人，改變了設計選擇？","SDG 17 · Partnerships for the Goals.":"SDG 17 · 夥伴關係。","Knowledge-sharing can improve a design. An interview, mentorship and a formal partnership describe different relationships.":"知識共享能改善設計。訪談、導師指導與正式合作，描述的是不同關係。","We will evaluate this channel as reach and dialogue: what people save, ask or challenge. Those observations will inform future posts. Learning change needs a separate before-and-after assessment, so follower activity is not reported as a learning gain.":"我們會從觸及與對話評估此管道：人們收藏、提問或質疑了什麼。這些觀察將引導未來貼文。學習改變需要另行進行前後評估，因此不把追蹤者活動當作學習增益。","Region 02 · Mushroom-body calyx / integration":"區域 02 · 蘑菇體萼部／整合","At the mushroom-body calyx, projection-neuron input reaches Kenyon cells. Our second educational layer connects ideas that first arrived separately: how a receptor works, why a reader needs controls, and how an algorithm can turn patterns into a decision.":"在蘑菇體萼部，投射神經元的輸入到達 Kenyon 細胞。我們的第二層教育連結最初分別接觸的概念：受體如何運作、讀取器為何需要對照，以及演算法如何把模式轉為決策。","The self-paced curriculum follows one odor signal across the project. Five modules use a question, an explanation, an interactive activity and a short assessment to connect the next concept. Learners can start with any module and revisit their browser-local progress.":"自訂進度課程沿著同一個氣味訊號，走過整個專案。五個模組以提問、解釋、互動活動與短評量，逐步連結下一個概念。學習者可以從任何模組開始，也能回顧保存在自己瀏覽器的進度。","01 · Discover":"01 · 發現","From volatile molecules to receptor patterns.":"從揮發性分子，到受體模式。","02 · Question":"02 · 提問","Can a smell answer a safety question?":"氣味能回答安全問題嗎？","Practise the limits of heat, appearance and odor as evidence.":"練習辨認加熱、外觀與氣味作為證據的限制。","03 · Build":"03 · 建構","How could a cell become a sensor?":"細胞如何成為感測器？","Connect receptor, reporter and measurement.":"連結受體、報導蛋白與量測。","04 · Decode":"04 · 解碼","What does the pattern mean?":"這個模式代表什麼？","Use the fly circuit as an entry point into computational interpretation.":"以果蠅迴路作為理解運算解讀的起點。","05 · Decide":"05 · 決定","What should happen next?":"接下來應該怎麼做？","Use uncertainty, screening and confirmation to choose a responsible action.":"運用不確定性、篩檢與確認，選擇負責任的行動。","Enter the Learning Lab ↗":"進入學習實驗室 ↗","The modules and their assessment instruments are available now. A visitor's saved score is personal feedback; it is not automatically collected into a research dataset. Formal cohort outcomes remain to be evaluated.":"模組與評量工具目前已可使用。訪客儲存的分數是個人回饋，不會自動蒐集成研究資料集。正式群體學習成果仍待評估。","Region 03 · Mushroom-body output / exchange":"區域 03 · 蘑菇體輸出／交流","The last part of this map is about taking an explanation into a new setting. Industry visitors, neuroscience students and other iGEM teams bring different assumptions. Their questions reveal which links in our story need more work. The events below document that exchange; they are not controlled learning trials.":"地圖的最後一部分，是將解釋帶入新的場合。產業訪客、神經科學學生與其他 iGEM 團隊，都帶著不同假設。他們的問題，讓我們知道故事中的哪些連結仍需加強。下方活動記錄的是這些交流，不是受控學習試驗。","May 2026 · SynBioBeta":"2026 年 5 月 · SynBioBeta","Explaining the platform beyond our own university":"向大學以外的觀眾解釋平台","We presented AeroSense in the NextGen Bioleader / poster setting at SynBioBeta 2026. The audience included people working in industry and synthetic biology, so we had to explain where biology, optics and computation meet before discussing technical detail. The event tested how the platform reads to people who do not share our lab's starting assumptions.":"我們在 SynBioBeta 2026 的 NextGen Bioleader／海報場合展示 AeroSense。觀眾包括產業與合成生物學工作者，因此在討論技術細節前，必須先解釋生物、光學與運算的交會處。這項活動讓我們檢視，不共享實驗室起始假設的人會如何理解平台。","Taking AeroSense's platform story to SynBioBeta 2026.":"將 AeroSense 的平台故事帶到 SynBioBeta 2026。","The same team event photograph appears in Human Practices.":"同一張團隊活動照片也出現在人文實踐頁面。","A new audience for the same scientific question.":"同一個科學問題，面對新的觀眾。","Read our conference poster (PDF) ↗":"閱讀研討會海報（PDF）↗","September 2026 · China Medical University":"2026 年 9 月 · 中國醫藥大學","Start with the biology, then connect the engineering.":"先從生物學開始，再連結工程。","At Prof. Ching-Che Charng's home institution, we shared AeroSense in a neuroscience course. The session introduced synthetic biology, iGEM and the project to students whose background was closer to neuroscience than to synthetic-biology engineering. That changed our explanation: begin with the odor-sensing logic, then show why the receptor, reporter and reader each have a distinct job.":"我們在 Ching-Che Charng 教授任職學校的神經科學課程分享 AeroSense。活動向背景較接近神經科學、而非合成生物學工程的學生，介紹合成生物學、iGEM 與專案。這改變了說明方式：先談氣味感測邏輯，再展示受體、報導蛋白與讀取器為何各有不同任務。","Sharing the project in a neuroscience classroom.":"在神經科學課堂分享專案。","The same visit photograph appears in Human Practices.":"同一張參訪照片也出現在人文實踐頁面。","Discussion helped us practise a more accessible biological explanation.":"討論幫助我們練習更容易理解的生物學說明。","October 2026 · iGEM TAU":"2026 年 10 月 · iGEM TAU","Different teams, different ways to tell a research story.":"不同團隊，以不同方式講述研究故事。","We took part in the 2026 iGEM Teams Meetup organised by Tel Aviv University's iGEM team. Teams from the Americas, Europe and Asia explained their work in different ways. The exchange gave us another audience for our project and a chance to compare how teams connect a problem, a design and a claim.":"我們參加由特拉維夫大學 iGEM 團隊主辦的 2026 iGEM Teams Meetup。來自美洲、歐洲與亞洲的團隊，以不同方式介紹研究。這場交流為專案帶來另一群觀眾，也讓我們比較各團隊如何連結問題、設計與主張。","Reusable now · teacher packet in preparation":"目前可重用 · 教師教材包準備中","Leave an activity someone else can run.":"留下別人也能帶領的活動。","The Learning Lab, games and educator protocol provide the current reusable materials. The planned teacher toolkit will bring a lesson guide, slides and worksheets together in one packet. Until that packet is complete, the links below point to the resources that already exist.":"學習實驗室、遊戲與教育者流程，是目前可重用的教材。規劃中的教師工具包，將整合教案、投影片與學習單。在套件完成前，下方連結先提供已存在的資源。","Use the teaching resources ↗":"使用教學資源 ↗","What we can learn from the next round":"下一輪能學到什麼","We have built activities, published teaching content and taken the project into new settings. The next question is what a learner can explain or decide afterward. We will score only paired responses from the same anonymous participant, report missing responses and keep age groups and instruments separate. A new transfer question will help distinguish remembering an answer from applying an idea.":"我們已建立活動、發布教學內容，並將專案帶入新場合。下一個問題是：學習者之後能解釋或決定什麼？我們只計分同一匿名參與者的配對回覆，報告缺答情形，並將年齡組別與評量工具分開。新的遷移應用題，將幫助區分記住答案與運用概念。","Three kinds of evidence answer different questions: participation tells us who took part, discussion tells us what people asked, and a matched assessment can show what changed. We will use them together without converting one into another.":"三種證據回答不同問題：參與記錄說明誰曾參與，討論說明人們問了什麼，配對評量則可顯示改變了什麼。我們會共同使用三者，但不把其中一種轉換成另一種。","What each activity is intended to teach":"每項活動預期教會什麼","Learning objectives mapped to lesson and game activities, proposed assessment items and the available evidence. Published learning materials are distinguished from completed participant assessment; no paired-cohort learning gain is claimed.":"將學習目標對應至課程與遊戲活動、提議的評量題目，以及現有證據。已發布教材與已完成的參與者評量分開呈現；未宣稱有配對群體的學習增益。","Learning objective":"學習目標","Activity / mechanic":"活動／機制","Assessment":"評量","Evidence and limitation":"證據與限制","Explain odor as a pattern across channels":"解釋氣味是跨通道模式","Module 1":"模組 1","pattern matching under noise":"雜訊下的模式配對","Module pre/post questions; game concept and transfer items":"模組前後測題目；遊戲概念題與遷移應用題","Lesson and game available; no completed paired cohort":"課程與遊戲可使用；無已完成的配對群體","Distinguish visible mold, heat treatment and toxin evidence":"區分可見黴菌、熱處理與毒素證據","Module 2":"模組 2","; household decision exercise":"；家庭決策練習","Early n = 28 summary informed content; no measured learning gain":"早期 n = 28 摘要引導內容；未量測學習增益","Separate receptor expression, reporter activity and a valid measurement":"區分受體表現、報導蛋白活動與有效量測","Module 3":"模組 3","; connect components":"；連結元件","Module pre/post and reflection":"模組前後測與反思","Published instrument; no scored cohort":"已發布評量工具；無已評分群體","Interpret a pattern without assuming perfect classification":"解讀模式，同時避免假設分類完美無誤","Module 4":"模組 4","overlapping mixtures":"重疊混合物","Module pre/post; game transfer question":"模組前後測；遊戲遷移應用題","Simplified teaching model; not a sensor-validation experiment":"簡化教學模型，不是感測器驗證實驗","Use uncertainty to choose a next action":"運用不確定性選擇下一步行動","Module 5":"模組 5","screening and confirmation decisions":"篩檢與確認決策","Module pre/post and separate reflection":"模組前後測與獨立反思","Available to try; no participant feedback export or real-world decision outcome":"可供體驗；無參與者回饋匯出檔或實際決策結果","Use limited scent information to choose a route":"利用有限氣味資訊選擇路徑","Odor Maze (Scentbound Labyrinth)":"氣味迷宮（Scentbound Labyrinth）",": find the exit; chests unlock scans, guidance and secret passages":"：找到出口；寶箱解鎖掃描、引導與秘密通道","No version-matched Maze assessment supplied; archived QC Shift G2 items do not measure this objective":"尚未提供與版本相符的迷宮評量；封存的 QC Shift G2 題目不量測此目標","Current maze is playable; no evaluated cohort or measured learning effect":"目前迷宮可遊玩；無已評估群體或實測學習效果","Matched pre/post results require the same anonymous session and instrument. We keep the food-safety items separate from olfactory-coding game scores; a shared topic does not make their scales interchangeable.":"配對前後測結果，需要同一匿名工作階段與評量工具。我們將食品安全題目與嗅覺編碼遊戲分數分開；主題相同，不代表量尺可以互換。","Playtest record":"遊玩測試記錄","No completed playtest session log or participant export has been supplied. The":"尚未提供已完成的遊玩測試場次記錄或參與者匯出檔。","existing playtest protocol":"既有遊玩測試流程","defines the next study. A report will include date, audience, game version, completed and paired counts, missing responses, observed problems and resulting revisions. Empty fields are not zero participants.":"定義下一次研究。報告將包含日期、觀眾、遊戲版本、完成人數與配對人數、缺答情形、觀察到的問題與後續修訂。空白欄位不等於零位參與者。","A live resource is evidence that something was built. It is not automatically evidence that learning improved.":"資源已上線，證明有人完成了建構，卻不會自動證明學習有所改善。","Learning, dialogue, and reach answer different questions. They are never added into one “impact” score.":"學習、對話與觸及回答不同問題，絕不加總成單一「影響力」分數。","Delivery status is not evaluation status. Color is not the only indicator.":"交付狀態不等於評估狀態；顏色也不是唯一指標。","Instrument":"工具","Delivery":"交付","Evaluation":"評估","Initial survey":"初期問卷","Early summary available":"可取得早期摘要","— raw export and updated analysis unavailable":"——無原始匯出檔與更新分析","Diagnostic only —":"僅供診斷——","counts & caveats":"人數與注意事項","Odor Pixel Suite":"氣味像素遊戲套組","Live":"已上線","Evaluation pending":"評估待進行","Playable is not educational effectiveness.":"可遊玩不等於具教育成效。","A live course is not a cohort result.":"課程已上線不等於有群體成果。","University workshop":"大學工作坊","Not yet evaluated":"尚未評估","A planned session cannot yield outcomes.":"規劃中的活動不能產生成果。","Elementary-school camp":"國小營隊","Social media":"社群媒體","Reach is not learning. Figures not reported yet.":"觸及不等於學習；尚未報告數據。","A · Learning":"A · 學習","for paired gain. No empty bar charts and no fabricated zeros.":"的配對增益。不使用空白長條圖，也不捏造零值。","What exists today is a":"目前已有的是","diagnostic":"診斷","and a":"與","method":"方法",", not a gain table.":"，而不是增益表。","Available now.":"目前可取得。","Early 28-response aggregate summary":"早期 28 份回覆的彙整摘要","; later 107-response total with no supplied item-level analysis.":"；後期總數 107，未提供逐題分析。","Instrument context":"工具背景",". No learning gain is claimed.":"。未宣稱有學習增益。","Method ready, no cohort.":"方法已備妥，尚無群體。","Learning Lab same-item pre/post per module. Odor Pixel optional study mode with paired items, transfer items, and anonymous JSON/CSV export. Workshop/camp not yet run.":"學習實驗室各模組使用相同題目前後測。Odor Pixel 選用研究模式提供配對題目、遷移應用題，以及匿名 JSON／CSV 匯出。工作坊／營隊尚未舉辦。","Planned measure":"預定量測","Paired pre/post":"配對前後測","Unit":"單位","Individual item ID / paired participant when both scored answers exist":"個別題目 ID／同時有兩次有效計分答案時的配對參與者","Knowledge or decision change on those items, in percentage points":"這些題目上的知識或決策變化，以百分點表示","A short-term post-test does not establish long-term retention. Same-item tests can partly measure familiarity with the sentence.":"短期後測不能確立長期保留效果。相同題目測試可能部分量到的是對句子的熟悉度。","B · Dialogue":"B · 對話","Dialogue is participant questions, qualitative feedback, educator notes, or design suggestions that reached the team. Page views, clicks, likes, and game completion are not dialogue.":"對話是參與者的問題、質性回饋、教育者筆記，或傳達給團隊的設計建議。瀏覽量、點擊、按讚與遊戲完成次數不是對話。","No completed participant-feedback redesign cycle has yet been reported.":"尚未報告已完成的參與者回饋—重新設計循環。","No consented quotes, observation cards, or workshop notes are published.":"未公布經同意的引言、觀察卡或工作坊筆記。","University workshop and elementary camp are the planned dialogue settings.":"大學工作坊與國小營隊是規劃中的對話場合。","On-wiki discussion prompts are teaching aids, not a record of what anyone said.":"網站 上的討論提示是教學輔助，不是任何人發言的記錄。","C · Reach":"C · 觸及","Reach is not learning.":"觸及不等於學習。","Traffic is not knowledge gain.":"流量不等於知識增益。","Social Reach, Engagement, and Learning evidence:":"社群觸及、互動與學習證據：","Not reported yet":"尚未報告","— not zero.":"——並非零。","Game-visit analytics: not reported.":"遊戲造訪分析：未報告。","Resource downloads: no downloadable teacher file exists on this wiki yet, so no download count.":"資源下載：此 網站 尚無可下載的教師檔案，因此沒有下載次數。","Open access to the playable suite and the live Lab is a":"公開開放可遊玩的套組與已上線的學習實驗室，是","delivery":"交付","fact, not a participant count.":"事實，不是參與者人數。","Privacy: the Learning Lab and game study mode do not collect names, emails, or learner IDs. See":"隱私：學習實驗室與遊戲研究模式不蒐集姓名、電子郵件或學習者 ID。詳見","Safety · Data and privacy":"安全 · 資料與隱私","Assessment methods, instruments and reusable resources":"評量方法、工具與可重用資源","Food-safety decisions and olfactory / synthetic-biology literacy are different jobs. We reuse item IDs where the job is the same. We do not add the two chains into a single learning-gain number.":"食品安全決策與嗅覺／合成生物學素養，是不同的任務。任務相同時，我們重用題目 ID；不把兩條路徑加總為單一學習增益數字。","Each node is a delivery fact plus an evaluation fact. Evidence view (above) adds scanning labels. The path itself does not change.":"每個節點同時包含交付事實與評估事實。上方證據檢視增加了方便掃讀的標籤，路徑本身並未改變。","Chain A · Food-safety decision literacy":"路徑 A · 食品安全決策素養","Evidence available":"有可用證據","Reuse":"重用","Canonical item IDs":"標準題目 ID","A3 · Lab":"A3 · 學習實驗室","Learning Lab Module 2":"學習實驗室模組 2","Workshop / camp pre–post":"工作坊／營隊前後測","Dialogue":"對話","Paired outcome analysis":"配對成果分析","Bridge · AeroSense Learning Lab":"橋梁 · AeroSense 學習實驗室","Lab":"學習實驗室","One curriculum, two jobs":"一套課程，兩種任務","Module 2 feeds Chain A. Modules 1, 3, 4, and 5 feed Chain B. Do not pool those scores.":"模組 2 對應路徑 A；模組 1、3、4、5 對應路徑 B。不要合併這些分數。","Chain B · Olfaction and synthetic-biology literacy":"路徑 B · 嗅覺與合成生物學素養","B2 · Lab":"B2 · 學習實驗室","Modules 1, 3, 4, 5":"模組 1、3、4、5","Workshop / camp discussion":"工作坊／營隊討論","Conceptual / participation outcomes":"概念／參與成果","A1 · Initial survey":"A1 · 初期問卷","Audience":"對象","Delivery / Evaluation":"交付／評估","Completed · Evidence available (diagnostic only).":"已完成 · 有可用證據（僅供診斷）。","Survey status and sample caveats:":"問卷狀態與樣本注意事項：",". Storage / risk / trust modules:":"。儲存／風險／信任模組：","Survey instrument":"問卷工具","The same chains, as a list":"相同路徑的清單版本","This list is the complete method. The diagram above is a scanning aid. JavaScript is not required to read it.":"這份清單是完整方法。上方圖示僅協助掃讀，不需 JavaScript 也能閱讀。","A2 · Canonical misconception item IDs":"A2 · 標準迷思題目 ID","Educational question":"教育問題","Can later tools score the same three food-safety claims, so results can be compared?":"後續工具能否對相同三項食品安全說法計分，讓結果可以比較？","Instrument designers, educators, and future iGEM teams.":"評量工具設計者、教育工作者與未來 iGEM 團隊。","Instrument / activity":"工具／活動",", and":"，以及","in":"，位於","js/learning-data.js":"js/learning-data.js","What is measured":"量測什麼","Nothing by itself. This node is the shared schema that makes Chain A comparable across survey, Module 2, and a future workshop pre–post.":"本身不量測任何成果。此節點是共用綱要，讓問卷、模組 2 與未來工作坊前後測中的路徑 A 可以比較。","Live (source on this wiki)":"已上線（原始碼在此 網站）","Not yet evaluated as a cohort instrument":"尚未作為群體評量工具進行評估","Stable IDs and wording. No paired correction table.":"固定的 ID 與題目文字；無配對答題修正表。","Shared IDs enable comparability. They do not prove that learners changed. They are not used as Odor Pixel scores.":"共享 ID 讓結果可比較，但不能證明學習者改變了，也不作為 Odor Pixel 分數。","A3 · Learning Lab Module 2":"A3 · 學習實驗室模組 2","After a structured lesson, does a visitor reject the same three food-safety claims?":"完成有結構的課程後，訪客是否會否定相同三項食品安全說法？","Self-paced wiki visitors. No identified cohort.":"自訂進度的 網站 訪客，沒有已界定的群體。","Module 2 · If it looks fine, is it safe?":"模組 2 · 看起來沒問題，就安全嗎？","Same-item pre/post.":"相同題目前後測。","Change on the three canonical Chain A items, stored in this browser only.":"三項標準路徑 A 題目的變化，只儲存在此瀏覽器。","The live module and item IDs. No published class average.":"已上線模組與題目 ID；無已公布的班級平均值。","A live lesson is not a validated gain. Local scores are not a sample. Same-item pre/post can partly measure familiarity with the original wording.":"課程已上線不等於增益已驗證。本機分數不是研究樣本。相同題目前後測，可能部分量到對原始題目文字的熟悉程度。","A4 · Educator-mode / workshop / camp pre–post":"A4 · 教育者模式／工作坊／營隊前後測","Do facilitated audiences change on the same Chain A items when a teacher is in the room?":"在教師引導下，參與者對相同路徑 A 題目的回答是否改變？","Planned lower-year undergraduates; planned elementary-school camp. None published.":"規劃中的低年級大學生與國小營隊；皆未公布成果。","Module 2 and/or game educator-mode pre–post with anonymous export, once a session runs.":"活動執行後，使用模組 2 及／或遊戲教育者模式的前後測與匿名匯出。","Paired item-level correction on the canonical food-safety IDs, if that instrument is the one used in the room.":"若現場使用該工具，則量測標準食品安全 ID 的逐題配對答題修正。","None. Date, partner, and headcount are not inserted.":"無。不填入未取得的日期、夥伴與人數。","Educator-mode existing in a product is not a completed deployment. Game educator-mode is not automatically a Chain A instrument unless it uses these items.":"產品中有教育者模式，不代表已完成實際使用。遊戲教育者模式若未使用這些題目，就不會自動成為路徑 A 工具。","A5 · Paired outcome analysis":"A5 · 配對成果分析","Did the residual heat and look/smell habits actually move after teaching?":"教學之後，對加熱與外觀／氣味仍存的習慣是否真正改變？","A future consented cohort. None exists on this wiki.":"未來經同意的群體；此 網站 目前沒有。","Planned paired analysis of the canonical IDs. If collection permits, one parallel transfer item per concept (not yet written up as data).":"規劃對標準 ID 進行配對分析。若資料蒐集允許，每個概念另設一題平行遷移應用題（尚未作為資料發表）。","Pre/post change on Chain A claims. Transfer items, if added, would test generalization beyond the original sentence. No such results exist.":"路徑 A 說法的前後測變化。若加入遷移應用題，可測試是否能超越原始句子而泛化；目前沒有此類結果。","None. We do not invent paired rates.":"無。我們不捏造配對比例。","The analysis plan is not an outcome. Same-item gains can overstate learning if people only recognize the survey sentence.":"分析計畫不是成果。如果人們只是認出問卷句子，相同題目的增益可能高估學習。","Can one open curriculum serve both jobs without mixing their measurements?":"同一套開放課程，能否同時服務兩種任務，又不混合其量測？","Self-paced wiki visitors; future educators using on-wiki discussion prompts.":"自訂進度的 網站 訪客，以及未來使用 網站 討論提示的教育工作者。","Five-module":"五模組",". Module 2 = Chain A. Modules 1, 3, 4, 5 = Chain B.":"。模組 2＝路徑 A；模組 1、3、4、5＝路徑 B。","Per-module pre/post on that module’s items. Chain A and Chain B scores should not be summed.":"每個模組各自題目的前後測。路徑 A 與路徑 B 分數不應加總。","The live course, printable discussion prompts, and item bank. No cohort table.":"已上線課程、可列印討論提示與題庫；無群體結果表。","A bridge is an architecture. It is not proof that either chain produced learning. Live is not validated.":"橋梁是一種架構，不是任一條路徑已產生學習效果的證明。上線不等於驗證。","B1 · Odor Pixel Suite":"B1 · 氣味像素遊戲套組","Can a visitor treat a smell as a pattern across receptors, including mixtures — not as one private switch?":"訪客能否把氣味視為跨受體的模式，包含混合氣味，而不是一種氣味對應一個專用開關？","Adults and children; Junior–Challenge levels.":"成人與兒童；初階至挑戰難度。","Three browser games at":"三款瀏覽器遊戲位於",". Optional workshop study mode uses":"。選用的工作坊研究模式使用",". Everyday visitors are not quizzed.":"。一般訪客不需作答測驗。","Olfactory coding, pattern recognition, and mixture decoding. This is not the food-safety survey construct unless a future instrument is shown to use those items.":"嗅覺編碼、模式辨識與混合物解碼。除非未來工具證實使用了那些題目，否則這不是食品安全問卷所量測的構念。","Live (external hub)":"已上線（外部入口）","The live hub, documented learning objectives, and the suite’s educator pack. No playtest cohort, no paired rates.":"已上線入口、有文件記錄的學習目標與套組教育者教材包；無遊玩測試群體，也無配對比例。","A shipped game is not a published learning gain. Do not read game scores as mycotoxin-misconception correction.":"遊戲已發布不等於學習增益已發表。不要把遊戲分數解讀成真菌毒素迷思的修正。","B2 · Learning Lab Modules 1, 3, 4, and 5":"B2 · 學習實驗室模組 1、3、4、5","Can a visitor follow AeroSense from combinatorial smell, through a living sensor and a decoder, to a screening decision that is not a verdict?":"訪客能否沿著 AeroSense，從組合式嗅覺、活體感測器與解碼器，一路理解到「篩檢決策不是最終判定」？","Self-paced wiki visitors.":"自訂進度的 網站 訪客。",", each with its own three-item pre/post.":"，各自具有三題前後測。","Olfaction, heterologous sensing, pattern decoding, and responsible action language — Chain B concepts, not the three kitchen-safety claims.":"嗅覺、異源感測、模式解碼與負責任的行動用語：這些是路徑 B 概念，不是三項廚房安全說法。","Live modules. No published cohort.":"模組已上線；無已公布群體。","Unidentified visitors. Browser-local scores are not a sample.":"未識別身分的訪客；瀏覽器本機分數不是研究樣本。","B3 · Workshop / camp hands-on discussion":"B3 · 工作坊／營隊實作討論","Can students talk through and try this science with other people, not only click a page?":"學生能否與他人一起討論並嘗試這些科學，而不只是點擊頁面？","Planned university workshop with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo; planned elementary-school camp.":"規劃與 Chung-Chuan Lo 教授合作的大學工作坊，以及國小營隊。","Hands-on session using the games and, where age-appropriate, Lab modules.":"使用遊戲的實作活動，並依年齡適切性加入學習實驗室模組。","Participation and facilitated discussion. Not a published dialogue record yet.":"參與與引導式討論；尚無已公布的對話記錄。","None. No quotes, photos, or attendance.":"無。沒有引言、照片或出席人數。","A planned conversation is not dialogue evidence.":"規劃中的對話，不是對話證據。","B4 · Conceptual / participation outcomes":"B4 · 概念／參與成果","After taking part, do students explain combinatorial smell, a living sensor, or screening-versus-verdict more carefully?":"參與後，學生能否更謹慎地解釋組合式嗅覺、活體感測器，以及篩檢與判定的區別？","Future workshop and camp cohorts.":"未來工作坊與營隊群體。","Planned conceptual and participation measures on Chain B ideas. Not the Chain A myth IDs unless that session actually uses them.":"規劃針對路徑 B 概念進行概念與參與量測。除非活動實際使用路徑 A 迷思 ID，否則不採用那些題目。","Nothing published. No outcome numbers are shown.":"尚無公布內容，不呈現成果數字。","None.":"無。","We do not invent conceptual-gain percentages. Chain B will not be reported as food-safety correction.":"我們不捏造概念增益百分比，也不將路徑 B 報告為食品安全觀念修正。","Why identical wording — and why that is not enough":"為何使用相同文字，以及為何仍然不夠","Benefit.":"優點。","On Chain A, Module 2 reuses the survey’s three statements with the same item IDs. That is for":"在路徑 A 中，模組 2 使用問卷相同的三個陳述與題目 ID，目的是","cross-instrument comparability":"跨工具可比性",": a diagnostic baseline and a later pre/post can be read against each other instead of against three unrelated quizzes.":"：讓診斷基準與後續前後測能相互對照，而不是比較三份毫無關聯的測驗。","Caution.":"注意。","Same-item pre/post testing can partly measure familiarity with the original sentence. If a future consented cohort is collected, we recommend one parallel “transfer” item per concept — a new wording of the same idea — to test whether learning generalizes. No transfer-item results exist, and none are shown.":"相同題目前後測可能部分量到對原始句子的熟悉度。若未來蒐集經同意的群體資料，我們建議每個概念加入一題平行「遷移」題，以不同措辭呈現相同概念，測試學習能否泛化。目前沒有遷移題結果，因此也未呈現任何結果。","Odor Pixel Suite is not in that wording match. Its teaching target is olfactory coding. Comparability across Chain A instruments does not license a combined “education impact” score with Chain B.":"氣味像素遊戲套組不屬於這組文字配對，其教學目標是嗅覺編碼。路徑 A 工具可比較，不代表可以與路徑 B 合併成「教育影響力」分數。","Iteration":"迭代","The right-hand column matters more than a generic outreach summary: what did evidence change in our education design?":"右欄比一般性的推廣摘要更重要：證據究竟改變了教育設計的什麼？","A completed arrow is shown only when a real redesign occurred. Internal design reviews are labeled as such. They are not participant quotes.":"只有實際發生重新設計，才顯示已完成的箭頭。內部設計審查會清楚標示，不當成參與者引言。","What learners may learn from us":"學習者可能從我們這裡學到什麼","Intended outcomes of live artifacts. These are teaching aims, not measured gains.":"已上線成果的預期成效。這些是教學目標，不是實測增益。","Track A.":"路線 A。","Reconsider the residual heat and look/smell food-safety claims (Module 2).":"重新思考仍存的加熱與外觀／氣味食品安全說法（模組 2）。","Track B.":"路線 B。","Treat odor as a pattern; see a living-sensor idea; interpret screening without treating it as a verdict (Lab 1, 3–5; Odor Pixel Suite).":"將氣味視為模式、理解活體感測器概念，並在解讀篩檢時不將其視為最終判定（學習實驗室 1、3–5；氣味像素遊戲套組）。","Participate.":"參與。","Planned workshop and camp. Not yet available.":"規劃中的工作坊與營隊，目前尚未提供。","What we learn from learners":"我們從學習者身上學到什麼","Documented education-design iterations only.":"僅列有記錄的教育設計迭代。","Evidence.":"證據。","Early n = 28 aggregate record":"早期 n = 28 彙整記錄",": 27/28 rejected the mold-removal claim, 24/28 the heat claim and 23/28 the look/smell claim. These are reported counts from the team narrative, not a reanalysis of a raw export.":"：27/28 否定移除黴菌的說法，24/28 否定加熱說法，23/28 否定外觀／氣味說法。這些是團隊敘述回報的人數，不是重新分析原始匯出檔的結果。","Change made.":"已做的改變。","Focused Track A on decision-related misconceptions instead of generic awareness.":"將路線 A 聚焦於與決策相關的迷思，而非一般性認知宣導。","Where it appears.":"出現位置。","This page;":"本頁；","; shared item IDs.":"；共享題目 ID。","Status.":"狀態。","Completed education-design iteration. Learning-gain evaluation still pending.":"已完成教育設計迭代；學習增益評估仍待進行。","Internal review after the games existed: odor-as-pattern play does not cover biology → engineering → computation → decision.":"遊戲完成後的內部審查：將氣味視為模式的遊戲，尚未涵蓋生物學 → 工程 → 運算 → 決策。","Interpretation.":"解讀。","A playable suite is not a full AeroSense pathway.":"可遊玩的套組，不等於完整 AeroSense 路徑。","Built the five-module Learning Lab alongside the games, with Module 2 matched to the survey items.":"在遊戲之外建立五模組學習實驗室，模組 2 與問卷題目對應。","Completed internal design iteration. Not a participant-feedback cycle.":"已完成內部設計迭代，不是參與者回饋循環。","Curriculum-writing constraint: a screening band is easy to read as a certificate.":"課程撰寫限制：篩檢分級容易被當成證明書。","Risk language can over-claim even when the science sentence is careful.":"即使科學敘述謹慎，風險用語仍可能過度宣稱。","Module 5 states that screening is not confirmatory testing and should trigger a next action, not a verdict.":"模組 5 明確說明，篩檢不是確認性檢測，應引導下一步行動，而不是作出最終判定。","Completed education-material change. Treating that sentence as a finished device UI is a separate, later evaluation — not claimed as a hardware redesign from this page.":"已完成教育材料修改。把這句話視為已完成的設備介面，屬於另一項較晚的評估；本頁不宣稱它已促成硬體重新設計。","No workshop, camp, or playtest export is published.":"尚未公布工作坊、營隊或遊玩測試的匯出資料。","Instruments can exist before audiences do.":"工具可以先於參與者群體存在。","None from participant feedback. The arrow stops here.":"尚無來自參與者回饋的改變；箭頭在此停止。","Where it would appear.":"未來會出現的位置。","Future Module / game copy, after a real export and notes.":"取得實際匯出資料與筆記後，更新模組／遊戲文案。","Education iteration model":"教育迭代模型","Assume":"假設","Completed. We assumed broad mold-risk misunderstanding.":"已完成。我們原本假設大眾普遍誤解黴菌風險。","Diagnose":"診斷","Completed. Initial survey.":"已完成。初期問卷。","Completed for current educational artifacts (two tracks, games, Lab, item IDs).":"目前教育成果已完成設計（兩條路線、遊戲、學習實驗室與題目 ID）。","Deliver":"交付","Games playable; Learning Lab live. Workshop and camp planned.":"遊戲可遊玩，學習實驗室已上線；工作坊與營隊規劃中。","Measure":"量測","Formal cohort evaluation pending.":"正式群體評估仍待進行。","Listen":"聆聽","Pending structured cohort feedback.":"等待有結構的群體回饋。","Revise":"修訂","Next evidence-based redesign pending.":"下一次依據證據的重新設計仍待進行。","Not just the lessons we built — but how someone else can run them.":"不只提供我們建立的課程，也說明其他人如何帶領。","Only resources that actually exist are listed. There is no Download button on a missing file. The linked game build, protocols and question bank are included in this wiki. Their published iGEM routes must be checked after deployment.":"僅列出實際存在的資源，不為缺失檔案放上下載按鈕。連結的遊戲版本、流程與題庫皆包含在此 網站 中；部署後仍須檢查其正式 iGEM 網址。","Resource manifest. Availability is a delivery fact. Evaluation status is separate.":"資源清單。可取得是交付事實，評估狀態另外呈現。","Resource":"資源","Format":"格式","Availability":"可用狀態","Reuse notes":"重用備註","Interactive olfactory-pattern education (three playable games)":"互動式嗅覺模式教育（三款可遊玩的遊戲）","General visitors; school / workshop learners":"一般訪客；學校／工作坊學習者","Browser suite":"瀏覽器遊戲套組","Live / playable":"已上線／可遊玩","· included in this wiki":"· 包含在此 網站 中","Next validation":"下一步驗證","Everyday visitors play immediately. Not official iGEM hosting yet.":"一般訪客可直接遊玩，目前尚非正式 iGEM 託管。","Suite educator record · includes archived Game 2":"套組教育者記錄 · 包含封存的遊戲 2","Educator overview and study workflow; QC Shift content is historical and does not describe the current Maze":"教育者概覽與研究流程；QC Shift 內容屬歷史記錄，不描述目前的迷宮","Facilitators":"活動帶領者","/education/":"/education/","Results empty":"結果空白","From PinChe567/iGEM-game. Game 2's QC Shift record is archived; no matched Maze outcome is available. Results fields stay empty until a real export.":"來自 PinChe567/iGEM-game。遊戲 2 的 QC Shift 記錄已封存，尚無相符的迷宮成果。在取得實際匯出資料前，結果欄位保持空白。","Education study protocol":"教育研究流程","Optional workshop study mode: paired pre/post, local export, how to count paired n":"選用工作坊研究模式：配對前後測、本機匯出，以及配對 n 的計算方式","Educators / research-style deployment":"教育工作者／研究形式的使用","Markdown":"Markdown","education-study-protocol.md":"education-study-protocol.md","Method documented; no cohort":"方法已記錄，尚無群體","Casual play does not use this protocol. Facilitators enable study mode; hub Play cards do not.":"一般遊玩不使用此流程。由活動帶領者啟用研究模式，入口的遊玩卡片不會啟用。","Question bank":"題庫","Conceptual item IDs and transfer items; G2 is archived QC Shift content":"概念題目 ID 與遷移應用題；G2 為封存的 QC Shift 內容","Facilitators analyzing exports":"分析匯出資料的活動帶領者","question-bank.md":"question-bank.md","No scored cohort":"無已評分群體","Traceable IDs. Do not recode answers to invent improvement.":"ID 可追溯。不要重新編碼答案以捏造進步。","Data dictionary / export schema":"資料字典／匯出綱要","Reproduce anonymous session fields, JSON/CSV export, paired-n rules":"重現匿名工作階段欄位、JSON／CSV 匯出與配對 n 規則","Facilitators / other iGEM teams":"活動帶領者／其他 iGEM 團隊","data-dictionary.md":"data-dictionary.md","Schema only":"僅有綱要","Storage key":"儲存鍵",". Empty cells mean missing, not zero. No PII fields.":"。空白欄位代表缺失，不是零；沒有個人識別資料欄位。","Playtest protocol":"遊玩測試流程","How to run a session and what not to collect":"如何執行一場活動，以及不應蒐集哪些資料","playtest-protocol.md":"playtest-protocol.md","Protocol; no filled session":"流程文件；尚無填妥的活動記錄","From PinChe567/iGEM-game":"來自 PinChe567/iGEM-game","Per-game facilitator notes":"各遊戲的帶領者筆記","Game-specific educator copy":"各遊戲專用的教育者說明","· pack":"· 教材包","Pending":"待完成","Files":"檔案",". Odor Maze (Scentbound Labyrinth) is the current Game 2.":"。氣味迷宮（Scentbound Labyrinth）是目前的遊戲 2。","and G2 question-bank items are archived QC Shift materials, not matched Maze teaching or assessment tools.":"與題庫 G2 題目，皆為封存的 QC Shift 教材，不是與目前迷宮相符的教學或評量工具。","Self-paced biology → engineering → decision curriculum":"自訂進度的生物學 → 工程 → 決策課程","Self-paced learners; educators":"自訂進度學習者；教育工作者","Wiki pages":"網站 頁面","Live on this wiki":"已在此 網站 上線","learning-platform.html":"learning-platform.html","Five modules, any order. Local store":"五個模組，可任意排序。本機儲存","Module 2 / survey item IDs":"模組 2／問卷題目 ID","Cross-instrument Track A comparison":"跨工具的路線 A 比較","Educators measuring food-safety claims":"量測食品安全說法的教育工作者","Live lesson +":"已上線課程＋","learning-02-mold.html":"learning-02-mold.html","IDs stable; no paired cohort":"ID 已固定；無配對群體","On-wiki discussion prompts":"網站 上的討論提示","Classroom talk after a module":"模組後的課堂討論","Educators":"教育工作者","HTML on the Lab":"學習實驗室中的 HTML","On-wiki":"網站 上提供","Learning Lab educator pack":"學習實驗室教育者教材包","Teaching aid, not dialogue evidence":"教學輔助，不是對話證據","Not a downloadable file. No Download button.":"不是可下載檔案，因此沒有下載按鈕。","Personal dashboard / local schema":"個人儀表板／本機資料綱要","Visitor can see their own pre/post in this browser":"訪客可在此瀏覽器查看自己的前後測","Self-paced learners":"自訂進度學習者","Wiki page + JS":"網站 頁面＋JS","progress.html":"progress.html","Not a study dataset":"不是研究資料集",". Nothing is sent until a consented backend exists.":"。在建立經同意的後端之前，不會傳送任何資料。","Teacher toolkit (guide, slides, worksheets)":"教師工具包（指南、投影片、學習單）","Printable classroom packet":"可列印的課堂教材包","Teachers":"教師","In preparation":"準備中","· no file":"· 尚無檔案","No placeholder download. See":"不提供占位下載。詳見","Reusable graphics / QR pack":"可重用圖像／QR 碼套件","Screenshots, GIFs, QR codes":"截圖、GIF、QR 碼","Wiki / classroom":"網站／課堂","Not in this repository":"此儲存庫未提供","Do not invent paths.":"不捏造檔案路徑。","For educators: optional study mode":"給教育工作者：選用研究模式","Casual visitors play the suite immediately. There is no mandatory pre-test on the public Play path. That is the default learner experience.":"一般訪客可直接遊玩套組。公開遊玩路徑沒有強制前測；這是預設的學習者體驗。","A separate workshop study mode can add paired measurement. For Game 2, the archived QC Shift G2 items do not match the current maze; they must not be interpreted as a Maze learning-gain measure. A matched Maze protocol remains to be developed. Facilitators follow the":"另設的工作坊研究模式可加入配對量測。對遊戲 2 而言，封存的 QC Shift G2 題目與目前迷宮不符，不得解讀為迷宮學習增益量測。相符的迷宮流程仍待開發。活動帶領者依照","education study protocol":"教育研究流程",": two short pre questions, the usual game, the same concepts after play plus one transfer item, optional feedback, then anonymous JSON (source of truth) and optional CSV. Answers stay in that browser. Nothing is transmitted automatically.":"：兩題簡短前測、一般遊戲、遊玩後測試相同概念並增加一題遷移應用題、選用回饋，再匯出匿名 JSON（主要依據）與選用 CSV。答案保留在該瀏覽器，不會自動傳送。","How to turn the mode on is documented in that protocol, not as this page’s primary play button.":"如何開啟此模式，記錄在該流程中，而不是本頁的主要遊玩按鈕。","View educator resources":"查看教育者資源","Run this yourself":"自己帶領活動","A reproducible workflow for another team. Casual game play does not require steps 4–8. The evaluation workflow is optional for educators and workshops.":"供其他團隊重現的流程。一般遊玩不需要步驟 4–8；評估流程是教育工作者與工作坊的選用項目。","Choose the audience (general public, elementary, university, self-paced).":"選擇對象（一般大眾、國小、大學、自訂進度學習者）。","Define the learning objective (Track A decision claims, or Track B olfactory / synbio ideas — not both as one score).":"定義學習目標（路線 A 的決策說法，或路線 B 的嗅覺／合成生物學概念；不將兩者合為一個分數）。","Select the relevant Learning Lab module and/or Odor Pixel game.":"選擇相關的學習實驗室模組及／或 Odor Pixel 遊戲。","If evaluation is intended, administer the pre-instrument (Lab quiz, or game study mode).":"若要進行評估，先施測前測工具（學習實驗室測驗或遊戲研究模式）。","Run the activity.":"進行活動。","Administer the paired post-instrument.":"施測配對後測工具。","Match responses using the documented anonymous / item-ID workflow. Paired":"依文件所述的匿名／題目 ID 流程配對回覆。配對","counts only sessions with scored pre and post for the same ID. Do not impute missing posts.":"僅計入同一 ID 同時有可計分前測與後測的工作階段。不補值缺失的後測。","Report exact denominators and limitations. Empty is not zero.":"報告確切分母與限制。空白不是零。","Collect qualitative feedback separately from anonymous JSON. Do not merge with class lists.":"質性回饋與匿名 JSON 分開蒐集，不與班級名冊合併。","Change the educational material only if evidence supports a redesign, and log it.":"只有在證據支持重新設計時，才修改教育材料，並留下記錄。","Why shared item IDs — and why that is not enough":"為何共享題目 ID，以及為何仍然不夠","See":"詳見","for the same-item / transfer caution. Game study mode already includes transfer IDs; no transfer-item results are reported here.":"關於相同題目／遷移應用的注意事項。遊戲研究模式已包含遷移題 ID；此處未報告遷移題結果。","Teach it yourself":"自己教學","Conference poster · PDF":"研討會海報 · PDF","Facilitator study guide":"活動帶領者研究指南","Export dictionary":"匯出資料字典","Discussion prompts":"討論提示","Early survey aggregates":"早期問卷彙整","A dedicated slide deck, print-and-play adaptation, original survey form and packaged teacher worksheets are not yet available. The live Module 2 items reproduce the three diagnostic claims; they do not replace the original four-module survey instrument. Wiki-authored content follows the site’s CC BY 4.0 notice; third-party assets and game software retain their own notices.":"專用投影片、列印遊玩改編版、原始問卷及套裝教師學習單，目前尚未提供。已上線模組 2 題目重現三項診斷說法，但不能取代原始四模組問卷工具。網站 原創內容遵循網站的 CC BY 4.0 聲明；第三方素材與遊戲軟體保留各自的授權聲明。","Limits":"限制","These are the bounds of the claim, not an apology for building the tools.":"這些界定的是主張範圍，不是為建立工具而致歉。","Initial survey sample caveats and item-level analysis status:":"初期問卷樣本注意事項與逐題分析狀態：",". Not a population prevalence or learning-gain study.":"。這不是人口盛行比例或學習增益研究。","Exact-item pre/post may create familiarity effects. Transfer-item results are not available — see":"完全相同題目的前後測可能產生熟悉效應。遷移題結果尚未取得；詳見","measurement caution":"量測注意事項","An immediate post-test, when it exists, will not establish long-term retention.":"即使未來有立即後測，也不能確立長期保留效果。","Social engagement does not establish learning. Reach figures are not reported yet.":"社群互動不能證明學習；觸及數據尚未報告。","Live Odor Pixel Suite / Learning Lab ≠ educational effectiveness. The second game is Odor Maze (Scentbound Labyrinth). The archived QC Shift guide and G2 questions do not assess the current maze.":"氣味像素遊戲套組／學習實驗室已上線，不等於具有教育成效。第二款遊戲是氣味迷宮（Scentbound Labyrinth）；封存的 QC Shift 指南與 G2 題目，不評估目前的迷宮。","Planned workshop and camp cannot yet provide outcome evidence. Different age groups will not be pooled as one equivalent cohort.":"規劃中的工作坊與營隊尚不能提供成果證據。不同年齡組別，不會合併為一個等效群體。","Survey and Module 2 share food-safety items; games teach olfactory coding / mixture decoding. We will not report a single correction rate across instruments unless items actually match.":"問卷與模組 2 共用食品安全題目；遊戲則教嗅覺編碼／混合物解碼。除非題目確實相符，否則不會跨工具報告單一答題修正率。","This Education wiki page provides fixed English and Traditional Chinese translations. The game suite is bilingual (zh-Hant / English). No separate bilingual teacher packet is published on this wiki.":"本教育 網站 頁面提供固定的英文與繁體中文譯文。遊戲套組為雙語（繁體中文／英文）。此 網站 尚未發布獨立的雙語教師教材包。","The next delivery round brings the existing materials to facilitated audiences, then evaluates paired responses and a transfer question. Attendance, consent arrangements, versioned materials and exact paired denominators will accompany any outcome claim. Recovering the original survey export and verifying the later 107-response total remain separate tasks.":"下一輪交付會將既有教材帶到有引導的觀眾群體，再評估配對回覆與一題遷移應用題。任何成果主張都會附上出席記錄、同意安排、具版本的教材與確切配對分母。找回原始問卷匯出檔，以及核實後期 107 份回覆總數，仍是獨立工作。","Planned · Xinfeng, Hsinchu":"規劃中 · 新竹新豐","For younger learners, we plan shorter concepts, visual comparisons and guided play. The aim is to help a child explain how a pattern can carry information and why a result can still be uncertain.":"對年幼學習者，我們規劃更簡短的概念、視覺比較與引導式遊玩。目標是幫助孩子解釋模式如何攜帶資訊，以及為何結果仍可能不確定。","The current plan identifies Xinfeng, Hsinchu. A confirmed activity record, attendance, photographs and learning outcomes are still to be added. Participation and any photographs will follow school and guardian arrangements.":"目前規劃地點為新竹新豐。已確認的活動記錄、出席人數、照片與學習成果仍待補入。參與及任何照片使用，皆將遵循學校與監護人的安排。","Planned · with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo":"規劃中 · 與 Chung-Chuan Lo 教授合作","Computational neuroscience workshop":"計算神經科學工作坊","For high-school-to-university learners, the planned workshop moves from biological inspiration to model reasoning. Participants will connect an odor-response pattern to coding, noise and a classifier's limits, using the curriculum and games as discussion material.":"面向高中至大學學習者的規劃工作坊，將從生物靈感走向模型推理。參與者會以課程與遊戲作為討論材料，將氣味反應模式連結至編碼、雜訊與分類器的限制。","The format is planned with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo. A completed workshop and measured learning effect are not yet part of this record.":"活動形式正與 Chung-Chuan Lo 教授共同規劃。已完成的工作坊與實測學習效果，尚未納入此記錄。","The next technical carousels, short science videos and printable teacher packet will follow the same assessment map. No effect is inferred from a published activity alone.":"下一批技術輪播圖、科學短影片與可列印教師教材包，都將依循同一評量地圖。不會僅憑活動已發布，就推論其效果。","Three stages of the education journey":"教育旅程的三個階段","Survey limitation":"問卷限制","Open full-size image: AeroSense Instagram educational carousel explaining the living odor-sensor concept.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense Instagram 教育輪播圖，解釋活體氣味感測器概念。","AeroSense Instagram educational carousel explaining the living odor-sensor concept.":"AeroSense Instagram 教育圖卡，說明活細胞氣味感測器的概念。","Open full-size image: A second graphic from the AeroSense Parts Design Instagram teaching carousel.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense 元件設計 Instagram 教學輪播圖的第二張圖。","A second graphic from the AeroSense Parts Design Instagram teaching carousel.":"AeroSense 元件設計 Instagram 教學輪播圖的第二張圖。","Open full-size image: AeroSense team at the SynBioBeta 2026 poster presentation.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense 團隊於 SynBioBeta 2026 海報展示。","AeroSense team at the SynBioBeta 2026 poster presentation.":"AeroSense 團隊於 SynBioBeta 2026 海報展示。","Open full-size image: Team photograph from SynBioBeta 2026.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：SynBioBeta 2026 團隊合照。","Team photograph from SynBioBeta 2026.":"SynBioBeta 2026 團隊合照。","Open full-size image: AeroSense guest lecture in a neuroscience course at China Medical University.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense 於中國醫藥大學神經科學課程的客座演講。","AeroSense guest lecture in a neuroscience course at China Medical University.":"AeroSense 於中國醫藥大學神經科學課程的客座演講。","Open full-size image: Students and presenters during the China Medical University session.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：中國醫藥大學課程中的學生與講者。","Students and presenters during the China Medical University session.":"中國醫藥大學課程中的學生與講者。","Learning objectives, activities and assessment":"學習目標、活動與評量","Delivery versus evaluation":"交付與評估的區別","Assume, diagnose, design, deliver, measure, listen, revise":"假設、診斷、設計、交付、量測、聆聽、修訂","Reusable education resource manifest":"可重用教育資源清單","Education · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026":"教育 · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026","Our survey shifted teaching from general mold awareness to decisions about invisible risks. The latest team record reports 300 respondents. We connect its findings to practical choices, classroom activities and reusable teaching materials.":"問卷讓教學從一般黴菌知識轉向看不見的風險判斷。團隊最新記錄報告 300 份回覆。我們將這些發現連結至實際選擇、課堂活動及可重用教材。","Updated from the team’s Education record · 18 October 2026.":"依團隊 Education 記錄更新 · 2026 年 10 月 18 日。","Read the source record":"閱讀來源記錄","Latest survey · team-reported n = 300":"最新問卷 · 團隊報告 n = 300","The bilingual online questionnaire asked about mold and mycotoxins, storage habits and screening-tool expectations. Respondents chose to take part. The latest summary reports the percentages below; it does not supply a response-level export, item-level denominators or collection dates.":"雙語線上問卷涵蓋黴菌與黴菌毒素、儲存習慣及篩檢工具需求，受訪者自行選擇參與。最新摘要報告以下百分比，未提供逐份回覆匯出檔、各題有效分母或蒐集日期。","Understanding differs across three risk concepts":"三種風險概念的理解程度不同","Risk concept":"風險概念","Reported understanding":"報告的理解比例","Removing visible mold does not always make food safe":"去除可見黴菌不一定使食物安全","Heating does not always destroy all mycotoxins":"加熱不一定能破壞所有黴菌毒素","Normal appearance and smell do not establish no risk":"外觀與氣味正常不能證明沒有風險","For the look-and-smell item, 27% were unsure and 15% held the misconception. These are reported percentages, not reconstructed response counts.":"外觀與氣味題中，27% 不確定，15% 持有迷思。此處呈現來源報告的百分比，未反推回覆人數。","The higher-knowledge group (n = 180) and lower-or-uncertain-knowledge group (n = 120) reported recording an opening date at 42% versus 25%, and a recommended storage practice at 71% versus 46%. Even in the higher-knowledge group, 58% did not record the opening date. These associations prompted teaching about habits alongside facts; they do not show that knowledge caused the behavior.":"知識較高組（n = 180）與知識較低或不確定組（n = 120）報告記錄開封日期的比例為 42% 與 25%，採取建議儲存方式則為 71% 與 46%。即使在知識較高組，仍有 58% 未記錄開封日期。這些關聯促使教學同時關注習慣與知識，但不能證明知識造成了行為改變。","Screening-tool priorities were trustworthiness (76%), accuracy including avoiding false negatives (73%), clear next-step guidance (68%), ease of use (61%), affordable cost per test (54%) and speed (49%). We therefore teach what a screening result can establish and how to act on uncertainty.":"篩檢工具需求為結果可信度（76%）、包含避免偽陰性的準確度（73%）、明確下一步指引（68%）、操作容易（61%）、可負擔的單次成本（54%）及速度（49%）。因此，我們說明篩檢結果能支持什麼判斷，以及如何面對不確定性。","The archived n = 28 snapshot below remains separate. The latest n = 300 summary does not identify overlapping responses, so the records are not pooled or treated as a before/after comparison. Neither sample estimates prevalence across Taiwan or measures learning gain.":"以下 n = 28 的封存摘要保留為獨立記錄。最新 n = 300 摘要未說明回覆重疊情形，因此不合併，也不視為前後測比較。兩者都不能估計全臺盛行比例或衡量學習增益。","Archived diagnostic snapshot · 23 August 2026":"封存診斷摘要 · 2026 年 8 月 23 日","The early n = 28 record and latest team-reported n = 300 summary are separate diagnostic records. Neither demonstrates population prevalence or learning gain.":"早期 n = 28 記錄與團隊最新報告的 n = 300 摘要為獨立診斷資料，皆不能證明人口盛行比例或學習增益。","Odor Maze (Scentbound Maze)":"氣味迷宮（Scentbound Maze）","Our design record describes five stages: draft design, internal refinement, public playtesting, camp/workshop deployment and data release. The October camp documents a classroom adaptation. Listing a stage in that template does not demonstrate that its playtest or evaluation is complete.":"設計記錄分為初稿、內部修訂、公開試玩、營隊／工作坊使用及資料發布五個階段。10 月營隊記錄了全班共同遊玩的改編；模板列出某個階段，不代表其試玩或評估已完成。","The technical series follows an odor signal through the living sensor, decoding model and hardware. Parts Design introduces the receptor and fluorescent reporter; the hardware post explains reading a faint signal against background noise.":"技術系列沿著活體感測器、解碼模型及硬體追蹤氣味訊號。Parts Design 介紹受體與螢光報導蛋白；硬體貼文說明如何從背景雜訊中讀取微弱訊號。","Reported reach and quiz participation":"報告的觸及與測驗參與","The team reports more than 1,700 accounts reached by feed posts, more than 1,400 by stories and more than 500 by reels, about 50 likes per post on average, and more than 100 new followers. These audiences may overlap, so reach is not added together.":"團隊報告貼文觸及超過 1,700 個帳號、限時動態超過 1,400、短影片超過 500；每則貼文平均約 50 個讚，新增追蹤者超過 100。各類觀眾可能重疊，因此不將觸及數加總。","More than 50 people answered the Sustainability Pop Quiz, with about 75% correct on average. This is a reported quiz result, not a paired learning-gain estimate. Most followers were aged 20–30. Reach and satisfaction show interest; they do not establish understanding or retention.":"超過 50 人回答永續小測驗，平均正確率約 75%。這是團隊報告的測驗結果，不是配對學習增益估計。追蹤者以 20–30 歲為主。觸及與滿意程度呈現興趣，不能證明理解或長期保留效果。","12 October 2026 · Shan-chi Elementary School":"2026 年 10 月 12 日 · 山崎國小","A science camp in Xinfeng":"新豐科學營隊","We ran a half-day camp for more than thirty pupils in grades 5 and 6 at Shan-chi Elementary School in Xinfeng, Hsinchu. A ten-minute mini-class linked three questions: how a nose smells, how an electronic nose works and what our laboratory is building.":"我們於新竹新豐山崎國小，為三十多位五、六年級學生舉辦半日營隊。約十分鐘的小課程串起三個問題：鼻子如何聞味道、電子鼻如何運作，以及我們的實驗室在做什麼。","We adapted Odor Pixel Suite for a whole class: projected questions let teams answer together by holding up one, two or three fingers. A short drawing and worksheet session followed the game.":"我們將 Odor Pixel Suite 改為全班共同參與：投影題目，讓各組以一、二或三根手指同時作答。遊戲後接續簡短繪畫與學習單活動。","We collected 22 worksheets. Thirteen children named something they had learned; nine described enjoyment only. Five mentioned the electronic nose and five mentioned the game; those mentions are not treated as mutually exclusive categories. Some described smell as tiny molecules or connected smelling to the brain.":"我們收回 22 份學習單。13 位孩子寫出具體學到的內容，9 位只描述開心或喜歡活動。其中 5 位提及電子鼻，5 位提及遊戲；這些提及項目不視為互斥類別。有些孩子將氣味描述為微小分子，或將嗅覺與大腦連結。","One learner found the memory game difficult and another commented on the number of questions. These short, self-reported reflections document engagement and teaching needs. They are not a scored pre/post assessment or proof of retention.":"一位學習者覺得記憶遊戲困難，另一位提到題目很多。這些簡短自述呈現參與情形與教學需求，並非計分前後測，也不能證明長期保留效果。","14 October 2026 · NTHU":"2026 年 10 月 14 日 · 清華大學","From the Brain to the Electronic Nose":"從大腦到電子鼻","With Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo, we ran an olfactory neuroscience workshop for the NTHU College of Life Science and Medicine. Fifteen participants attended: five doctoral, five master’s and five bachelor’s students.":"我們與羅中泉教授合作，為清華大學生命科學暨醫學院舉辦嗅覺神經科學工作坊，共 15 人參加：博士班、碩士班與學士班各 5 人。","Prof. Lo introduced receptor binding, combinatorial odor coding and the fly’s antennal lobe and mushroom body. We connected that biology to the living-cell sensor and classifier, demonstrated a Learning Lab module and invited participants to try the online platform.":"羅教授介紹受體結合、組合式氣味編碼，以及果蠅觸角葉與蕈狀體。我們將生物原理連結至活細胞感測器與分類器，示範一個 Learning Lab 模組，並邀請參與者試用線上平台。","The feedback summary reports positive satisfaction and perceived understanding. Participants also found some English technical terms difficult and requested a clearer take-home message, neural-network explanation, project goal and intended use. The source provides no numerical satisfaction scale or paired knowledge scores.":"回饋摘要報告正向滿意度與自覺理解提升。參與者也指出部分英文術語難以理解，希望更清楚的重點整理、神經網路說明、專案目標與使用情境。來源未提供滿意度數值量表或配對知識分數。","The team reports more than 500 people using the Learning Lab. This is a participation summary, not an audited completion count or learning-gain result. The intended pace is about eight minutes per module, around forty minutes in total.":"團隊報告超過 500 人使用 Learning Lab。這是參與摘要，並非經稽核的完課數或學習增益結果。建議節奏為每模組約八分鐘，總計約四十分鐘。","Learner feedback prompted shorter opening text, clearer color-separated sections, easier opening and closing activities, and more hands-on tasks. The modules remain reusable individually so teachers can adapt them to their own setting.":"學習者回饋促使我們縮短開場文字、以色塊清楚區分章節、降低開場與結尾活動難度，並增加操作任務。各模組仍可獨立重用，讓教師依自身情境改編。","At SynBioBeta in San Jose, 4–7 May 2026, we presented our poster through the Next-Gen BioLeaders program. Questions about living-cell scale, regulation and hardware exposed gaps in our explanation. A wet-lab researcher asked how the sensor itself is built. The exchange informed later consultations and our move toward agricultural and food-safety screening; a specific scaling follow-up is not yet documented.":"2026 年 5 月 4–7 日，我們透過 Next-Gen BioLeaders 計畫，在聖荷西 SynBioBeta 展示海報。關於活細胞規模化、法規及硬體的提問，指出說明中的缺口；一位濕實驗背景研究者也詢問感測器本身如何建立。交流影響了後續諮詢，以及轉向農業與食品安全篩檢的方向；具體規模化後續行動仍未記錄。","23 September 2026 · China Medical University":"2026 年 9 月 23 日 · 中國醫藥大學","At Prof. Ching-Che Charng’s invitation, a model-team member presented our electronic-nose work to more than thirty undergraduate and graduate students. The lecture connected sensor drift and recalibration to stable insect odor coding and our spiking neural network, while discussing limitations such as sensor redundancy and continuous-odor performance. Questions about how a sensor pattern becomes a decision led us to simplify the model introduction in the later NTHU workshop.":"應張景哲教授邀請，模型組成員向三十多位大學部與研究所學生分享電子鼻研究。演講將感測器漂移與重新校準，連結到昆蟲穩定的氣味編碼及我們的脈衝神經網路，同時討論感測器冗餘與連續氣味表現等限制。聽眾詢問感測模式如何變成決策，促使我們在後續清大工作坊簡化模型介紹。","8 October 2026 · iGEM TAU-Israel":"2026 年 10 月 8 日 · iGEM TAU-Israel","We joined the online Mini Jamboree hosted by iGEM TAU-Israel. The team record reports eight teams from six countries, with presentations of about fifteen minutes each. We shared our project and education activities, received model-design feedback and compared teaching approaches. Specific comments and resulting design changes remain to be documented.":"我們參與 iGEM TAU-Israel 主辦的線上 Mini Jamboree。團隊記錄報告來自六國的八支隊伍，每隊約十五分鐘簡報。我們分享專案與教育活動，收到模型設計回饋，並比較教學方式。具體評論及因此產生的設計修改仍待記錄。","Reusable now · teacher toolkit and education guide":"已可重用 · 教師工具包與教育指南","The school principal asked for materials teachers could keep using after our visit. Our toolkit combines lesson slides, the game and Learning Lab instructions. The education guide explains how another team can diagnose audience needs, choose a claim, match a format, evaluate it and hand the materials on.":"校長希望取得教材，讓教師能在我們到訪後持續使用。工具包整合課程投影片、遊戲與 Learning Lab 操作說明；教育指南則說明其他隊伍如何診斷觀眾需求、選擇主張、搭配形式、評估並移交教材。","Teacher toolkit instructions · PDF":"教師工具包說明 · PDF","Education planning guide · PDF":"教育規劃指南 · PDF","Source toolkit folder":"原始工具包資料夾","Creative output":"創作成果","The electronic nose in a learner’s imagination":"學習者想像中的電子鼻","Participants were invited to draw an electronic nose or fruit fly as they imagined it. Their drawings preserve a creative response to the activities. We present them as participant work, not as a validated measure of scientific understanding.":"我們邀請參與者畫出想像中的電子鼻或果蠅。這些作品保留了活動引發的創意回應；此處呈現參與者創作，不把它們當作經驗證的科學理解評量。","The game build, protocols and question bank are included in this wiki. The teacher toolkit instructions and education planning guide are now available as PDFs, with the source toolkit folder linked above.":"本 wiki 收錄遊戲、程序與題庫。教師工具包說明及教育規劃指南已提供 PDF，上方亦附原始工具包資料夾連結。","Teacher toolkit and education guide":"教師工具包與教育指南","Run a classroom session or plan a new education activity":"帶領課堂活動或規劃新教育活動","Teachers and future iGEM teams":"教師及未來 iGEM 隊伍","Toolkit instructions":"工具包說明","Education guide":"教育指南","Reusable materials; no paired outcome dataset":"可重用教材；尚無配對成果資料集","Adapt the audience, language and timing; retain the distinction between participation and learning evidence.":"依觀眾、語言與時間改編，並維持參與證據與學習證據的區分。","Participant feedback now informs revisions: Learning Lab users asked for less text and an easier entry point; CMU questions prompted a plainer model explanation in the October workshop. Camp worksheets and workshop feedback identify further teaching needs, while paired learning outcomes remain unpublished.":"參與者回饋已用於修訂：Learning Lab 使用者希望減少文字並降低入門難度；中國醫藥大學的提問促使 10 月工作坊採用更平易的模型說明。營隊學習單及工作坊回饋指出後續教學需求，配對學習成果仍未發布。","Read the October activity record":"閱讀 10 月活動記錄","The fly olfactory pathway used as a reading map for education.":"以果蠅嗅覺路徑作為教育章節閱讀地圖。","Team-reported survey understanding: visible mold, heating, and appearance or smell.":"團隊報告的問卷理解程度：可見黴菌、加熱，以及外觀或氣味。","Self-reported storage practices compared across two knowledge groups.":"兩個知識組別自述的儲存習慣比較。","Screening-tool priorities reported in the latest team survey summary.":"團隊最新問卷摘要報告的篩檢工具優先需求。","View the source survey graphics":"查看來源問卷圖表","Parts Design: odor molecules and receptor binding.":"Parts Design：氣味分子與受體結合。","Parts Design: the fluorescent signal as an educational diagram.":"Parts Design：以教學示意圖解釋螢光訊號。","Parts Design: connecting the cell signal to the next question.":"Parts Design：從細胞訊號連結到下一個問題。","A teaching diagram of the PN, KC and MBON decoding pathway.":"PN、KC 與 MBON 解碼路徑的教學示意圖。","Hardware carousel: introducing the optical reader.":"硬體輪播：介紹光學讀取器。","Hardware carousel: reading a faint signal in background noise.":"硬體輪播：從背景雜訊讀取微弱訊號。","Hardware carousel: explaining lock-in amplification.":"硬體輪播：說明鎖相放大。","Original hardware teaching graphic: an integrated-reader concept.":"原始硬體教學圖：整合讀取器概念。","The sustainability series invites readers to connect design choices with SDGs.":"永續系列邀請讀者將設計選擇連結至 SDGs。","Explore the teaching carousels":"瀏覽教學輪播圖","These are the original teaching graphics. Power and validation labels in the hardware concept graphic describe the team’s design presentation; they are not a whole-system power measurement or independent proof of validated performance.":"這些是原始教學圖。硬體概念圖中的功耗與驗證標籤呈現團隊的設計說明，不是整體系統功耗量測，也不是性能已驗證的獨立證據。","Shan-chi pupils explore familiar scents during the camp.":"山崎國小學生於營隊探索熟悉的氣味。","The mini-class connects the nose, electronic nose and AeroSense project.":"小課程串起鼻子、電子鼻與 AeroSense 專案。","Odor Pixel Suite adapted for a projected classroom activity.":"將 Odor Pixel Suite 改編為投影課堂活動。","Teams participate together in the camp’s game session.":"營隊遊戲時，各組共同參與。","Participants in the NTHU olfactory neuroscience workshop.":"清大嗅覺神經科學工作坊參與者。","Discussion during the workshop with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo.":"與羅中泉教授進行工作坊討論。","Presenting the project during the NTHU workshop.":"於清大工作坊介紹專案。","The online Mini Jamboree project exchange on 8 October 2026.":"2026 年 10 月 8 日線上 Mini Jamboree 專案交流。","Participant fruit-fly drawing 1 from the school camp.":"國小營隊參與者果蠅創作 1。","Participant fruit-fly drawing 2 from the school camp.":"國小營隊參與者果蠅創作 2。","Participant fruit-fly drawing 3 from the school camp.":"國小營隊參與者果蠅創作 3。","Participant fruit-fly drawing 4 from the school camp.":"國小營隊參與者果蠅創作 4。","Pixel Lab and Scent Mixer support optional study mode: paired pre/post and transfer questions, with anonymous JSON or CSV exported locally. The current Scentbound Maze has no study-mode pre/post or export hooks. Archived QC Shift G2 questions do not assess the Maze.":"Pixel Lab 與 Scent Mixer 支援選用研究模式：配對前後測及遷移題，並於本機匯出匿名 JSON 或 CSV。目前 Scentbound Maze 未接上研究模式前後測或匯出功能；封存的 QC Shift G2 題目不能評估迷宮。","Use the protocol to enable study mode only for the supported Pixel Lab and Scent Mixer games.":"請依程序文件，只在支援的 Pixel Lab 與 Scent Mixer 遊戲啟用研究模式。",". Optional study mode for Pixel Lab and Scent Mixer uses":"。Pixel Lab 與 Scent Mixer 的選用研究模式使用",". The current Maze does not support this study workflow. Casual play remains available.":"。目前迷宮不支援此研究流程，一般遊玩仍可使用。","The archived diagnostic record contains 28 responses and three aggregate item counts. A separate latest team summary reports 300 respondents.":"封存的診斷記錄含 28 份回覆與三項彙整計數；獨立的團隊最新摘要報告 300 位受訪者。","October activities now provide attendance records, learner reflections and feedback-driven teaching changes. No participant-level paired knowledge dataset is published here. The survey, social-media quiz and workshop feedback use different instruments and are not combined into one learning score.":"10 月活動已提供參與記錄、學習者反思與依回饋修訂的教學內容。此處尚未發布個人層級的配對知識資料集。問卷、社群測驗及工作坊回饋使用不同工具，不合併為單一學習分數。","Our early survey shifted teaching from general mold awareness to decisions about invisible risks. A later team summary now reports 300 respondents. We present the two records separately and connect their findings to practical choices, classroom activities and reusable teaching materials.":"早期問卷讓教學從一般黴菌知識轉向看不見的風險判斷。團隊後期摘要現報告 300 份回覆。我們分開呈現兩份記錄，並將發現連結至實際選擇、課堂活動及可重用教材。","Explore education activities through the fly-brain map":"從果蠅腦地圖探索教育活動","Choose a region. Follow your curiosity.":"選一個腦區，跟著好奇心出發。","A fly brain full of learning":"裝滿學習活動的果蠅腦","Eight colored regions link to our education activities. This illustrated navigation map is an educational metaphor, not a map of biological function.":"八個彩色區域連結至我們的教育活動。這張插畫導覽圖是教育比喻，不代表生物腦區的功能定位。","Public survey":"公眾問卷","Odor games":"氣味遊戲","Social posts":"社群貼文","Learning Lab":"Learning Lab","School camp":"國小營隊","University":"大學","workshop":"工作坊","Science exchange":"科學交流","Learner art":"學童創作","Activity links":"活動連結","Our activities, imagined as regions of a fly brain. Select a colored region to visit its activity. The shapes organize this education story; they do not assign these activities to biological brain functions.":"把我們的活動想像成果蠅腦的不同區域。選取彩色腦區即可前往對應活動；這些形狀用來組織教育故事，並不表示活動對應真實腦功能。","Original teaching diagram":"原始教學示意圖","Introduction":"引言","\"Everyone has the right to education.\" Universal Declaration of Human Rights, Article 26 [1]":"「人人都有受教育的權利。」 《世界人權宣言》第 26 條 [1]","\"Everyone has the right to education.\" Universal Declaration of Human Rights, Article 26":"「人人都有受教育的權利。」 《世界人權宣言》第 26 條","In 1948 the United Nations General Assembly adopted the Universal Declaration of Human Rights. Article 26 states that everyone has the right to education, that it shall be free at least in the elementary and fundamental stages, and that it \"shall be directed to the full development of the human personality and to the strengthening of respect for human rights and fundamental freedoms\" [1]. The 2030 Agenda carries the same commitment forward as Sustainable Development Goal 4, \"ensure inclusive and equitable quality education and promote lifelong learning opportunities for all\", and Target 4.7 asks that every learner gain the knowledge and skills needed to promote sustainable development [2].":"1948 年，聯合國大會通過《世界人權宣言》。第 26 條指出，人人都有受教育的權利，至少在初等和基本教育階段應予免費，而且教育「應以充分發展人的個性並加強對人權和基本自由的尊重為目的」[1]。《2030 年永續發展議程》透過永續發展目標 4，延續這項承諾：「確保包容和公平的優質教育，讓所有人享有終身學習機會」；目標 4.7 則要求每位學習者取得促進永續發展所需的知識與技能 [2]。","In 1948 the United Nations General Assembly adopted the Universal Declaration of Human Rights. Article 26 states that everyone has the right to education, that it shall be free at least in the elementary and fundamental stages, and that it \"shall be directed to the full development of the human personality and to the strengthening of respect for human rights and fundamental freedoms\"":"1948 年，聯合國大會通過《世界人權宣言》。第 26 條指出，人人都有受教育的權利，至少在初等和基本教育階段應予免費，而且教育「應以充分發展人的個性並加強對人權和基本自由的尊重為目的」",". The 2030 Agenda carries the same commitment forward as Sustainable Development Goal 4, \"ensure inclusive and equitable quality education and promote lifelong learning opportunities for all\", and Target 4.7 asks that every learner gain the knowledge and skills needed to promote sustainable development":"。《2030 年永續發展議程》透過永續發展目標 4，延續這項承諾：「確保包容和公平的優質教育，讓所有人享有終身學習機會」；目標 4.7 則要求每位學習者取得促進永續發展所需的知識與技能",".":"。","Access to information is not the same as education that changes what people do. Science-communication research has long questioned the \"deficit model\", the assumption that people hold mistaken views because they lack facts. Knowledge does shape attitudes, but the relationship is far more nuanced than the model assumes [3], and the model persists for reasons that include how scientists are trained and how they imagine their audiences [4]. Research on pro-environmental behavior documents the same distance between knowing and doing [5].":"能取得資訊，不等於接受了能改變人們行為的教育。科學傳播研究長期以來一直質疑「知識缺陷模型」：這個模型假設，人們之所以抱持錯誤觀點，是因為缺乏事實知識。知識確實會影響態度，但兩者的關係遠比模型所假設的細緻複雜 [3]；這個模型之所以持續存在，部分原因包括科學家接受訓練的方式，以及他們如何想像自己的受眾 [4]。促進環境保護行為的研究，也記錄了同樣的知行落差 [5]。","Access to information is not the same as education that changes what people do. Science-communication research has long questioned the \"deficit model\", the assumption that people hold mistaken views because they lack facts. Knowledge does shape attitudes, but the relationship is far more nuanced than the model assumes":"能取得資訊，不等於接受了能改變人們行為的教育。科學傳播研究長期以來一直質疑「知識缺陷模型」：這個模型假設，人們之所以抱持錯誤觀點，是因為缺乏事實知識。知識確實會影響態度，但兩者的關係遠比模型所假設的細緻複雜",", and the model persists for reasons that include how scientists are trained and how they imagine their audiences":"；這個模型之所以持續存在，部分原因包括科學家接受訓練的方式，以及他們如何想像自己的受眾",". Research on pro-environmental behavior documents the same distance between knowing and doing":"。促進環境保護行為的研究，也記錄了同樣的知行落差","Our own survey pointed the same way. Most respondents already understood that visible mold is a problem, so a lecture saying \"mold is dangerous\" would have repeated what many people knew. The gap was in the risks that cannot be seen: only 58% understood that a normal look and smell does not mean no risk, and even respondents with higher knowledge often did not act on it. We went looking for what the research suggests works instead: active learning raised exam performance by 0.47 standard deviations and lowered failure rates (21.8% against 33.8%) across 225 science, engineering, and mathematics studies [6], and in a meta-analysis of serious-games studies, serious games outperformed conventional instruction on learning (d = 0.29) and retention (d = 0.36), though they were not more motivating [7]. These studies come from formal courses, so we treat them as direction, not proof, and we test our own tools on our own audiences.":"我們自己的問卷也指向同樣的情況。大多數受訪者已經知道，看得見的黴菌是個問題，因此，一場宣導「黴菌很危險」的講座，只會重複許多人已經知道的事。缺口在於看不見的風險：只有 58% 的人理解，外觀與氣味正常並不代表沒有風險，而且即使是知識程度較高的受訪者，也經常沒有將知識付諸行動。我們因此開始尋找研究所提出的其他有效方法：在 225 項科學、工程與數學研究中，主動學習使考試表現提高了 0.47 個標準差，並降低不及格率（21.8%，相較於 33.8%）[6]；而一項嚴肅遊戲研究的統合分析顯示，嚴肅遊戲在學習（d = 0.29）與知識保留（d = 0.36）方面優於傳統教學，但並未帶來更高的學習動機 [7]。這些研究來自正式課程，因此我們將其視為方向，而非證明，並針對自己的受眾測試我們自己的工具。","Our own survey pointed the same way. Most respondents already understood that visible mold is a problem, so a lecture saying \"mold is dangerous\" would have repeated what many people knew. The gap was in the risks that cannot be seen: only 58% understood that a normal look and smell does not mean no risk, and even respondents with higher knowledge often did not act on it. We went looking for what the research suggests works instead: active learning raised exam performance by 0.47 standard deviations and lowered failure rates (21.8% against 33.8%) across 225 science, engineering, and mathematics studies":"我們自己的問卷也指向同樣的情況。大多數受訪者已經知道，看得見的黴菌是個問題，因此，一場宣導「黴菌很危險」的講座，只會重複許多人已經知道的事。缺口在於看不見的風險：只有 58% 的人理解，外觀與氣味正常並不代表沒有風險，而且即使是知識程度較高的受訪者，也經常沒有將知識付諸行動。我們因此開始尋找研究所提出的其他有效方法：在 225 項科學、工程與數學研究中，主動學習使考試表現提高了 0.47 個標準差，並降低不及格率（21.8%，相較於 33.8%）",", and in a meta-analysis of serious-games studies, serious games outperformed conventional instruction on learning (d = 0.29) and retention (d = 0.36), though they were not more motivating":"；而一項嚴肅遊戲研究的統合分析顯示，嚴肅遊戲在學習（d = 0.29）與知識保留（d = 0.36）方面優於傳統教學，但並未帶來更高的學習動機",". These studies come from formal courses, so we treat them as direction, not proof, and we test our own tools on our own audiences.":"。這些研究來自正式課程，因此我們將其視為方向，而非證明，並針對自己的受眾測試我們自己的工具。","Synthetic biology adds a second reason to engage. The Royal Academy of Engineering's early public dialogue on the field called for an active and ongoing public engagement programme, with platforms for people to share their views on both the benefits and the concerns [8]. AeroSense puts a fly olfactory receptor into a cultured human cell line and reads it with a fly-inspired circuit. We wanted people to understand that, and to tell us what they thought of it.":"合成生物學為公眾參與增添了第二個理由。英國皇家工程院早期針對此領域舉辦的公眾對話，呼籲建立積極且持續的公眾參與計畫，提供平台，讓人們分享對其益處與疑慮的看法 [8]。AeroSense 將果蠅嗅覺受體放入培養的人類細胞株，並透過受到果蠅啟發的電路讀取訊號。我們希望人們理解這件事，也希望聽到他們對此的想法。","Synthetic biology adds a second reason to engage. The Royal Academy of Engineering's early public dialogue on the field called for an active and ongoing public engagement programme, with platforms for people to share their views on both the benefits and the concerns":"合成生物學為公眾參與增添了第二個理由。英國皇家工程院早期針對此領域舉辦的公眾對話，呼籲建立積極且持續的公眾參與計畫，提供平台，讓人們分享對其益處與疑慮的看法",". AeroSense puts a fly olfactory receptor into a cultured human cell line and reads it with a fly-inspired circuit. We wanted people to understand that, and to tell us what they thought of it.":"。AeroSense 將果蠅嗅覺受體放入培養的人類細胞株，並透過受到果蠅啟發的電路讀取訊號。我們希望人們理解這件事，也希望聽到他們對此的想法。","Our Education Journey as The Fly Brain Map":"以果蠅腦地圖呈現我們的教育旅程","Antennal Lobe":"觸角葉","Public Survey — the diagnostic instrument":"公眾問卷——診斷工具","Online Games (Odor Pixel Suite) — the three-game intervention":"線上遊戲（Odor Pixel Suite）——三款遊戲構成的介入","Social Media, Short Video & Articles — the reach channel":"社群媒體、短影音與文章——觸及管道","Mushroom Body Calyx":"蘑菇體萼部","Elementary School Science Camp":"國小科學營","Olfactory Neuroscience Workshop":"嗅覺神經科學工作坊","AeroSense Learning Lab — the online curriculum":"AeroSense Learning Lab——線上課程","Mushroom Body Lobes / MBON":"蘑菇體葉部／蘑菇體輸出神經元（MBON）","SynBioBeta 2026 (Next-Gen BioLeaders and Poster Session)":"SynBioBeta 2026（Next-Gen BioLeaders 與海報發表）","Mini Jamboree":"Mini Jamboree","University Guest Lecture":"大學客座演講","Teacher Toolkit & Education Guide — open resources":"教師工具包與教育指南——開放資源","Art Exhibition — what participants made":"藝術展覽——參與者的創作","Antennal Lobe: input (broadest reach)":"觸角葉：輸入（最廣泛的觸及）","Biological meaning. The antennal lobe is the fly's primary olfactory processing center — roughly 50 anatomically distinct glomeruli, each wired to a single receptor type, where signal from thousands of olfactory sensory neurons first converges. Nothing is interpreted yet here; it's simply where every receptor channel's raw reading arrives in parallel. It's the literal starting point of \"a smell is a pattern across many channels\" — the idea our whole sensing platform, and Module 1 (Discover) of our online Learning Lab, is built on.":"生物學意義。觸角葉是果蠅的初級嗅覺處理中心——約有 50 個在解剖構造上各自獨立的嗅小球，每個嗅小球都連接至單一受體類型，數千個嗅覺感覺神經元的訊號在此首次匯聚。這裡尚未進行任何解讀；它只是每個受體通道的原始讀值平行抵達的地方。這正是「氣味是跨越許多通道的一組模式」的起點——我們整個感測平台，以及線上 Learning Lab 的模組 1（探索），都建立在這個概念之上。","How we reach this stage of education. We treat the AL as our broadest-reach layer. None of the three projects here are trying to teach anyone anything in depth — they're trying to find out what the widest possible audience already believes (Public Survey), get them to make a decision and see its consequence in under fifteen minutes (Online Games), or keep the same corrective claim in front of them through feeds, short videos, and articles they already read (Social Media, Short Video & Articles). Like the AL itself, breadth comes before interpretation.":"我們如何觸及這個教育階段。我們將觸角葉（AL）視為觸及範圍最廣的一層。這裡的三項計畫都不是要深入教授任何人任何內容——它們試圖了解盡可能廣泛的受眾已經抱持哪些看法（公眾問卷），讓人們在不到十五分鐘內做出決定並看見其結果（線上遊戲），或透過他們原本就會閱讀的動態消息、短影音與文章，持續將同一項澄清觀念的主張呈現在他們面前（社群媒體、短影音與文章）。如同觸角葉本身，廣度先於解讀。","1. Public Survey":"1. 公眾問卷","Why does it matter?":"為什麼重要？","Before designing any education, we needed to know what people actually believed about mold and mycotoxin risk, and whether knowing the facts changes what they do. We did not want to assume a knowledge gap and then build a solution for a problem that might not exist in the form we imagined.":"在設計任何教育內容之前，我們需要了解人們對黴菌與黴菌毒素風險實際抱持哪些看法，以及了解事實是否會改變他們的行為。我們不希望先假設存在知識缺口，再為一個可能並非以我們想像的形式存在的問題打造解決方案。","Educational Impact from us.":"我們帶來的教育影響。","We ran a bilingual (Chinese and English) online questionnaire on mold and mycotoxin understanding, food-storage habits and what people want from a screening tool. It reached 300 respondents. Three findings shaped the rest of our education work:":"我們進行了一份中英雙語線上問卷，調查人們對黴菌與黴菌毒素的理解、食物儲存習慣，以及他們對篩檢工具的需求。問卷共觸及 300 位受訪者。其中三項發現，形塑了我們其餘的教育工作：","Public understanding varies by risk concept. People were most secure about the risk they can see. 78% understood that removing visible mold does not always make food safe. Understanding was lower for heat, where 64% understood that heating does not always destroy all mycotoxins, and lowest for looks and smell, where only 58% understood that a normal look and smell does not mean no risk. On that last item 27% were unsure and 15% held the misconception. The risks that cannot be seen are the ones people understand least, and they are the risks our sensor is meant to address.":"公眾的理解程度因風險概念而異。對於看得見的風險，人們的認知最為確實。78% 的人理解，移除看得見的黴菌，不一定能讓食物變得安全。對加熱的理解程度較低，64% 的人理解，加熱不一定能破壞所有黴菌毒素；對外觀與氣味的理解程度最低，只有 58% 的人理解，外觀與氣味正常並不代表沒有風險。在最後這一題中，27% 的人不確定，15% 的人抱持錯誤觀念。看不見的風險，是人們理解最少的風險，也是我們的感測器希望處理的風險。","Knowledge does not automatically translate into practice. We compared respondents with higher knowledge (n = 180) with those with lower or uncertain knowledge (n = 120). Higher-knowledge respondents were more likely to record the opening date (42% against 25%) and to report a recommended storage practice (71% against 46%). But even in the higher-knowledge group, 58% did not record the opening date. Knowing the facts helped, but it did not close the gap between knowing and doing.":"知識不會自動轉化為實踐。我們比較了知識程度較高的受訪者（n = 180），以及知識程度較低或不確定的受訪者（n = 120）。知識程度較高的受訪者，更可能記錄開封日期（42%，相較於 25%），也更可能回報採取了建議的儲存做法（71%，相較於 46%）。然而，即使在知識程度較高的組別中，仍有 58% 的人沒有記錄開封日期。了解事實有所幫助，卻未能消除知與行之間的落差。","Users value trustworthy, actionable results. Asked what they need from a screening tool, respondents chose trustworthiness of results (76%) and accuracy, including avoiding false negatives (73%) first, followed by clear next-step guidance (68%). These ranked ahead of ease of use (61%), affordable cost per test (54%) and a fast result (49%). People do not only want a number; they want to trust it and know what to do next.":"使用者重視可信賴且能據以行動的結果。當被問及對篩檢工具的需求時，受訪者優先選擇了結果的可信度（76%），以及包含避免偽陰性在內的準確度（73%），其次是清楚的下一步指引（68%）。這些項目的排名，高於容易使用（61%）、可負擔的單次檢測成本（54%），以及快速取得結果（49%）。人們想要的不只是一個數字；他們希望能夠信任它，並知道接下來該怎麼做。","Impact on us.":"對我們的影響。","The survey changed what we built. Because understanding was weakest for invisible risks, we made the claim that heat and looks and smell cannot tell you whether food is safe the center of the game and of Module 2 of the Learning Lab, which use the same statements as the survey so that later results can be compared with this baseline. Because knowledge did not automatically become practice, we added habits, such as recording the opening date, to the curriculum and our posts alongside the facts. Because people want trust and a clear next step, the Learning Lab teaches what a screening result does and does not certify, and what to do after each result, and our design prioritizes avoiding missed risk.":"問卷改變了我們所打造的內容。由於人們對看不見的風險理解最薄弱，我們將「加熱、外觀與氣味無法告訴你食物是否安全」這項主張，作為遊戲與 Learning Lab 模組 2 的核心；兩者使用與問卷相同的敘述，讓後續結果能夠與這份基準比較。由於知識不會自動轉化為實踐，除了事實知識，我們也在課程與貼文中加入記錄開封日期等習慣。由於人們希望獲得信任與清楚的下一步，Learning Lab 教導篩檢結果能夠與不能夠證明什麼，以及取得每種結果之後該怎麼做，而我們的設計也優先考量避免漏掉風險。","What it cannot tell us.":"它無法告訴我們什麼。","These are self-reported answers from people who chose to respond, so they show where to look, not how common each belief or habit is across Taiwan.":"這些答案是由自行選擇參與的人自我回報，因此，它們呈現了值得關注的方向，而非每一種看法或習慣在全臺灣有多普遍。","2. Online Games — Odor Pixel Suite":"2. 線上遊戲——Odor Pixel Suite","The survey data above is exactly why a lecture wouldn't work here: the gaps it revealed — trusting a printed date instead of tracking when a pack was opened, and not being sure whether heat or a sniff test can be trusted — are decision habits, not missing facts, and habits don't move from being told something twice. We needed an experience where the learner makes the decision and sees what it costs, which is also why this design choice ties directly back to the Education loop and the project's own motivation rather than appearing out of nowhere.":"上述問卷資料，正是演講在這裡無法奏效的原因：它揭露的缺口——相信印在包裝上的日期，而不是記錄包裝何時開封，以及不確定加熱或聞氣味測試是否可信——屬於決策習慣，而非缺少事實知識，而習慣不會因為同一件事被告知兩次就改變。我們需要一種體驗，讓學習者親自做出決策，並看見代價；這也說明了為什麼這項設計選擇直接連結到教育回饋循環與專題本身的動機，而非憑空出現。","Odor Pixel Suite is three short games, built through a five-stage design journey. We report the journey as a template with the evidence each stage should produce:":"Odor Pixel Suite 包含三款短遊戲，經過五個階段的設計歷程建構而成。我們將這段歷程整理為範本，並列出每個階段應產生的證據：","Draft design":"草案設計","Internal playtest & refinement":"內部試玩與改進","Public playtest & feedback":"公開試玩與回饋","Camp/workshop deployment":"營隊／工作坊實施","Data + optional external release":"資料與選用的對外發布","3. Social Media":"3. 社群媒體","The survey and the game both need someone to seek them out: fill in a questionnaire, or sit down and play. Social media reaches the person who will do neither. It puts the same ideas in a feed people are already scrolling, trading depth for reach.":"問卷與遊戲都需要有人主動找上門：填寫問卷，或坐下來玩遊戲。社群媒體則能觸及兩者都不會做的人。它把相同的概念放進人們原本就在滑閱的動態消息中，以深度換取觸及。","We ran three series, each built for a different kind of reader.":"我們推出了三個系列，每個系列都為不同類型的讀者設計。","Series 1: From fly nose to edge device.":"系列 1：從果蠅鼻子到邊緣裝置。","Three posts that follow one smell through the AeroSense system, one post per layer: the living sensor, the decoding model, and the hardware. Each post is a short carousel written for readers with no biology or engineering background.":"三篇貼文跟隨一種氣味走過 AeroSense 系統，每篇介紹一個層次：活體感測器、解碼模型與硬體。每篇都是簡短的輪播貼文，為沒有生物學或工程背景的讀者撰寫。","Post 1, Parts Design: \"We put a fruit fly's nose inside a human cell.\" Explains how a fruit fly odor receptor and a calcium-sensitive glow protein, placed in human cells, turn a smell into light: an odor molecule binds the receptor, calcium flows in, and the cell lights up. The brighter the glow, the stronger the smell.":"貼文 1，元件設計：「我們把果蠅的鼻子放進人類細胞裡。」 說明放入人類細胞中的果蠅氣味受體與鈣敏感發光蛋白，如何將氣味轉變為光：氣味分子結合受體，鈣流入，細胞便亮起來。光越亮，氣味就越強。","Post 2, Model: \"The cell lit up. Now what?\" How a circuit modeled on the fruit fly brain turns the glow into a decision. Coming soon.":"貼文 2，模型：「細胞亮起來了。接下來呢？」 以果蠅腦為模型的神經迴路，如何將光轉化為決策。即將推出。","Post 3, Hardware: \"Hearing a cell's faint glow in a noisy room.\" How the edge device picks a faint signal out of background noise.":"貼文 3，硬體：「在吵雜的房間裡，聽見細胞微弱的光。」 邊緣裝置如何從背景雜訊中辨識出微弱訊號。","Series 2: Sustainability Pop Quiz.":"系列 2：永續發展隨堂測驗。","Four multiple-choice Instagram stories, each followed by an answer card. Every question ties one AeroSense design choice to a Sustainable Development Goal, so followers learn what the goals mean by guessing which one applies.":"四則選擇題形式的 Instagram 限時動態，每題之後都附上一張解答卡。每道題目都將 AeroSense 的一項設計選擇與一項永續發展目標連結起來，讓追蹤者透過猜測適用的目標，了解這些目標的意義。","Flagging a batch of bananas or mangoes before disease symptoms are visible points to SDG 2, Zero Hunger. An edge classifier under 1 W, with core logic from a paper our own team published, points to SDG 9, Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure. A reusable, non-destructive sensing cartridge points to SDG 12, Responsible Consumption and Production. And the interviews with an e-nose company's chief scientist, several biotech companies, and an analytical-instrumentation professor point to SDG 17, Partnerships for the Goals.":"在疾病症狀出現之前，標示出一批香蕉或芒果的風險，對應 SDG 2「消除飢餓」。功耗低於 1 W、核心邏輯來自我們團隊自己發表之論文的邊緣分類器，對應 SDG 9「產業、創新與基礎建設」。可重複使用、非破壞性的感測匣，對應 SDG 12「負責任的消費與生產」。而與電子鼻公司首席科學家、數家生技公司及分析儀器領域教授進行的訪談，則對應 SDG 17「夥伴關係」。","Impact on us. We treat social media as a reach channel, not a measurement tool. Over the posting period, our feed posts reached more than 1,700 accounts, our stories more than 1,400, and our reels more than 500, with an average of about 50 likes per post. We gained more than 100 new followers, and more than 50 people answered the Sustainability Pop Quiz stories, getting about 75% correct on average. Our best-performing post was Post 2, \"The cell lit up. Now what?\" Most of our audience was aged 20 to 30.":"對我們的影響。 我們將社群媒體視為觸及管道，而非衡量工具。在發文期間，我們的動態貼文觸及超過 1,700 個帳號、限時動態超過 1,400 個、Reels 短影音超過 500 個，每篇貼文平均約有 50 個讚。我們新增了超過 100 位追蹤者，超過 50 人回答了永續發展隨堂測驗限時動態，平均答對率約為 75%。表現最好的貼文是貼文 2：「細胞亮起來了。接下來呢？」大多數受眾的年齡介於 20 至 30 歲。","These numbers show interest, not learning. Saves, poll responses, and comment questions cannot tell us whether someone understood an idea, so we measure knowledge change where we can pair a before and an after: in the game and the Learning Lab. Our own observation from comparable in-person outreach, such as street booths and pub-quiz events, is that this kind of content tends to over-index on audiences who are already interested in science. The age data does not settle this, because it tells us who followed, not whether they were already interested in science.":"這些數字呈現的是興趣，而非學習。收藏、投票回應與留言提問，無法告訴我們一個人是否理解了某個概念，因此，我們在能夠配對前後結果的地方衡量知識變化：遊戲與 Learning Lab。我們從街頭攤位、酒吧問答活動等類似實體推廣活動中的觀察是，這類內容往往讓原本就對科學有興趣的受眾占比較高。年齡資料無法釐清這一點，因為它告訴我們的是誰追蹤了帳號，而非他們是否原本就對科學有興趣。","Mushroom Body Calyx: integration (structured learning)":"蘑菇體萼部：整合（有架構的學習）","Biological meaning.":"生物學意義。","The calyx is the dendritic input zone of the mushroom body — around 2,000 Kenyon cells receive sparse, combinatorial input here from antennal-lobe projection neurons, and this is where parallel receptor channels actually get bound together into one learnable, associative pattern. It's the integration step — the subject of Module 4 (Decode) of our curriculum — and biologically, it's where exposure becomes memory.":"萼部是蘑菇體的樹突輸入區——約 2,000 個 Kenyon 細胞在此接收來自觸角葉投射神經元的稀疏、組合式輸入，而平行的受體通道正是在這裡，被結合成一個能夠學習並建立聯結的模式。這是整合的步驟——也是我們課程模組 4（解碼）的主題——而在生物學上，這裡就是接觸轉化為記憶的地方。","How we reach this stage of education.":"我們如何觸及這個教育階段。","The three projects here have a different job than the first part's: they're not trying to reach as many people as possible, they're trying to turn a shorter exposure into real, structured understanding, across the full age range our work touches — elementary schoolers, university life-science and medical students, and a self-paced option open to anyone.":"這裡的三項計畫，承擔著與第一部分不同的任務：它們並非試圖觸及盡可能多的人，而是試圖將短暫的接觸轉化為真正、有架構的理解，涵蓋我們工作所接觸的完整年齡範圍——國小學童、大學生命科學與醫學領域的學生，以及向所有人開放、可自行安排進度的學習選項。","1. Elementary School Science Camp":"1. 國小科學營","Shan-chi Elementary School is a rural school in Xinfeng Township, Hsinchu County. Bringing a hands-on science session to a school there is a small step toward the equal access to quality education that SDG 4 describes. The camp also lets us test our claim that the game can be understood by children, instead of assuming it.":"山崎國小是位於新竹縣新豐鄉的一所鄉村學校。將動手實作的科學活動帶進當地學校，是朝向 SDG 4 所描述的平等取得優質教育機會邁出的一小步。這場營隊也讓我們能夠檢驗「兒童能理解這款遊戲」的主張，而非直接假設如此。","On October 12, 2026 we ran a half-day science camp at the school for more than thirty upper-grade pupils (grades 5 and 6).":"2026 年 10 月 12 日，我們在該校為三十多位高年級學童（五、六年級）舉辦了半天的科學營。","We started with a Science Mini-Class. In about ten minutes we asked three questions in a row: How does a nose smell? How does an electronic nose smell? And what does our lab do? Each answer built on the one before, so the children could follow a smell from their own nose, to a machine, to the sensor we are building.":"我們從科學小教室開始。在約十分鐘內，我們接連提出三個問題：鼻子如何聞到氣味？電子鼻如何聞到氣味？我們的實驗室又在做什麼？每個答案都建立在前一個答案之上，讓孩子們能循著氣味，從自己的鼻子一路理解到機器，再到我們正在打造的感測器。","Next, the children played Odor Pixel Suite, the game we designed, as a challenge that lasted about ten minutes. We adapted it for a whole class. Instead of one child at one screen, the questions were projected on a screen, and each team answered at the same time by holding up one, two, or three fingers.":"接著，孩子們透過我們設計的 Odor Pixel Suite 遊戲，進行約十分鐘的挑戰。我們將遊戲調整為適合全班參與的形式。每個孩子不再各自面對一個螢幕，而是將問題投影在螢幕上，讓每一組同時舉起一根、兩根或三根手指作答。","Then came a drawing and worksheet session of about fifteen minutes. The children drew a cartoon nose or a cartoon fruit fly, and completed a worksheet. The children's drawings are shown in the Art Exhibition section below.":"接下來是約十五分鐘的繪畫與學習單活動。孩子們畫出卡通鼻子或卡通果蠅，並完成一份學習單。孩子們的畫作展示於下方的藝術展覽章節。","We collected 22 worksheets from the camp, each asking what the child learned or felt. Thirteen children named something they had learned, and nine wrote only that they had fun or liked the game. Five wrote about the electronic nose, and five mentioned the game. One wrote that the memory game was \"really hard,\" and another noted that it had \"a lot of questions.\"":"我們從營隊中收集了 22 份學習單，每份都詢問孩子學到了什麼或有什麼感受。十三位孩子寫出了自己學到的內容，九位只寫了玩得很開心或喜歡這款遊戲。五位寫到了電子鼻，五位提到了遊戲。一位寫說記憶遊戲「真的很難」，另一位則提到它「有很多題目」。","Several children put the science in their own words. One wrote that everyday smells are made of many tiny molecules. Another wrote that different animals smell in different ways and that smelling uses the brain, not only the nose. A third wrote that we can use the brain in place of the nose. One wrote that technology is powerful and should be used to build the future, and one asked the school to hold the activity again.":"幾位孩子用自己的話表達了科學概念。一位寫道，日常氣味由許多微小分子組成。另一位寫道，不同動物聞氣味的方式不同，而且聞氣味會用到大腦，不只是鼻子。第三位寫道，我們可以用大腦代替鼻子。一位寫道，科技很強大，應該用來打造未來，還有一位希望學校再次舉辦這項活動。","This suggests that children could follow the path from nose to electronic nose and enjoyed the game, although the worksheets are short and self-reported, so they do not measure how much each child understood.":"這顯示孩子們能跟上從鼻子到電子鼻的理解路徑，也喜歡這款遊戲；不過，學習單內容簡短且屬於自我回報，因此無法衡量每位孩子理解了多少。","Perfume Smelling Event":"香水聞香活動","“What is Smell?” Lesson":"「什麼是氣味？」課程","‘Odor Pixel Suite’ Online Game Playing":"遊玩「Odor Pixel Suite」線上遊戲","2. Olfactory Neuroscience Workshop (with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo)":"2. 嗅覺神經科學工作坊（與羅中泉教授合作）","Few people outside the field know how an animal actually turns a smell into a decision, and that logic is exactly what our electronic nose borrows. The workshop put the original science and our engineering in the same room, so students could see the line from how a brain smells to how we design a sensor. It also gave us a first chance to check whether the full online chain, talk, project and game, works with students who are one step from choosing a field.":"在這個領域之外，很少有人知道動物實際上如何將氣味轉化為決策，而這套邏輯，正是我們的電子鼻所借鑑的。工作坊將原本的科學與我們的工程設計帶進同一個空間，讓學生看見從大腦如何聞到氣味，到我們如何設計感測器之間的連結。這也首次讓我們有機會檢驗，包含演講、專題與遊戲的完整線上流程，是否適合即將選擇專業領域的學生。","On October 14, 2026, we ran \"From the Brain to the Electronic Nose,\" a workshop for students of the NTHU College of Life Science and Medicine. Prof. Lo then spoke on the biological logic underneath olfaction: how receptors bind odor molecules, how a single smell is represented by a combination of receptors rather than one, and how the fly's antennal lobe and mushroom body turn that pattern into a decision. He also showed how this circuit-level understanding from computational neuroscience has inspired approaches to artificial intelligence.":"2026 年 10 月 14 日，我們為清華大學生命科學暨醫學院的學生舉辦了「從大腦到電子鼻」工作坊。隨後，羅教授講解了嗅覺背後的生物學邏輯：受體如何結合氣味分子，單一氣味如何由多個受體的組合而非一個受體來表徵，以及果蠅的觸角葉與蘑菇體如何將這個模式轉化為決策。他也展示了計算神經科學對這類神經迴路的理解，如何啟發人工智慧的方法。","We followed with introducing our project: why early detection of food mold and crop disease matters, how a living-cell sensor built from an olfactory receptor and a fluorescent reporter detects volatile compounds, and how a fly-brain-inspired classifier reads the resulting \"odor fingerprint.\" We closed that part with the idea that how biology smells is how we design. Then everyone tried our online platform. We gave a short tour of the Learning Lab, running one module live so that students could see how its five modules fit together. The workshop ended with a feedback form.":"接著，我們介紹自己的專題：為什麼及早偵測食物黴菌與作物疾病很重要，由嗅覺受體與螢光報導系統構成的活細胞感測器如何偵測揮發性化合物，以及受到果蠅腦啟發的分類器，如何讀取由此產生的「氣味指紋」。我們以「生物如何聞到氣味，就是我們如何設計」這個概念，作為這部分的結尾。之後，所有人都試用了我們的線上平台。我們簡短導覽了 Learning Lab，並現場進行其中一個模組，讓學生看見五個模組如何相互連結。工作坊最後以回饋表單收尾。","The workshop drew 15 participants, split evenly across doctoral, master's, and bachelor's students. Prof. Lo's talk received the highest satisfaction, and participants strongly agreed that they understood the olfactory mechanism and the electronic nose mechanism better after attending.":"工作坊共有 15 位參與者，博士生、碩士生與學士班學生的人數相同。羅教授的演講獲得最高的滿意度，而參與者也高度認同，參加後更了解嗅覺機制與電子鼻機制。","Their suggestions were specific. Some English technical terms were hard to follow, which made it difficult to understand the rest of the talk, remember where a term had appeared, and ask questions afterward. Participants wanted a take-home message that gives the overall picture of the project, and asked us to explain the neural network, the project goal, and the intended use more clearly.":"他們提出了具體的建議。有些英文專業術語難以理解，這使他們難以跟上演講其餘內容、記住某個術語曾出現在哪裡，以及在演講後提出問題。參與者希望有一段能帶走的重點摘要，呈現專題的整體樣貌，也希望我們更清楚地解釋神經網路、專題目標與預期用途。","3. AeroSense Learning Lab — the online curriculum":"3. AeroSense Learning Lab——線上課程","A camp or a workshop reaches the people in the room. We believe everyone should get the same chance to understand the science that affects their food, and that should not depend on living near a university. The Learning Lab lets anyone go through the whole chain at their own pace, from home: how a fly smells, how a living cell can be turned into a sensor, and what a screening result does and does not tell you.":"營隊或工作坊能觸及在場的人。我們相信，每個人都應該有同樣的機會，理解影響自己食物的科學，而這不應取決於是否住在大學附近。Learning Lab 讓任何人都能在家中，依照自己的步調走過完整的知識鏈：果蠅如何聞到氣味、如何將活細胞轉變為感測器，以及篩檢結果能夠與不能夠告訴你什麼。","Free to use online, with nothing to install":"可在線上免費使用，無須安裝任何東西","Five modules of about 8 minutes each, around 40 minutes in total, organized as Biology, then Engineering, then Decision":"五個模組，每個約 8 分鐘，總計約 40 分鐘，依序安排為生物學、工程，再到決策","Module 2 uses the same statements as our public survey, so learners' answers can be compared with our survey baseline":"模組 2 使用與公眾問卷相同的敘述，因此學習者的答案可以與我們的問卷基準比較","Printable discussion prompts for educators, and a teacher toolkit that other teams can build on":"提供教育者可列印的討論提示，以及可供其他團隊進一步延伸的教師工具包","Live at Learning Lab · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026":"已上線：Learning Lab · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026","We wrote it for self-learners from upper-secondary school onward, for university students, and for educators who want a ready-made lesson on olfaction and food safety. The modules can be taken in any order, but they are designed to follow the logic of the project itself, as listed below.":"我們為高中階段以上的自學者、大學生，以及希望取得現成嗅覺與食品安全課程的教育者撰寫了這套內容。模組可以依任何順序進行，但其設計是依循專題本身的邏輯，順序如下。","Discover. How animals smell: receptors binding odor molecules, and sparse, combinatorial coding in the fly antennal lobe and mushroom body.":"探索。動物如何聞到氣味：受體結合氣味分子，以及果蠅觸角葉與蘑菇體中的稀疏、組合式編碼。","Question. Mold versus mycotoxin risk, and why looks and smell cannot be trusted.":"提問。黴菌與黴菌毒素風險的差異，以及為什麼外觀與氣味不可靠。","Build. Expressing OR/Orco and GCaMP6 in cultured cells to make a self-renewing living sensor.":"建構。在培養細胞中表現 OR/Orco 與 GCaMP6，打造可自我更新的活體感測器。","Decode. A smell as a pattern across many receptors, and how fly-brain-inspired computation reads it.":"解碼。將氣味視為跨越多個受體的一組模式，以及受到果蠅腦啟發的計算方法如何讀取它。","Decide. Screening is not certified testing: risk tiers and the correct next action.":"決策。篩檢不等於經認證的檢測：風險分級與正確的下一步行動。","Each module ends with three check questions. The full set is in the teacher toolkit, described under Teacher Toolkit & Education Guide in Mushroom Body Lobes / MBON.":"每個模組最後都有三道檢核問題。完整題目收錄於教師工具包中，詳見「蘑菇體葉部／蘑菇體輸出神經元（MBON）」中的「教師工具包與教育指南」。","More than 500 people have gone through the Learning Lab. Because Module 2 reuses the survey's statements word for word, their answers can be compared with our survey baseline of 300 respondents.":"已有超過 500 人走過 Learning Lab 的學習內容。由於模組 2 逐字沿用問卷的敘述，他們的答案可以與我們包含 300 位受訪者的問卷基準比較。","Learners told us two things, and we changed the platform in response. First, the interface was unclear and the opening had too much text, so we cut the text and separated sections with color blocks to make the page easier to follow. Second, the opening was too difficult. To make the platform accessible to more people, we lowered the difficulty of the opening and closing sections and added hands-on tasks, so that learners understand by doing.":"學習者告訴我們兩件事，而我們據此調整了平台。首先，介面不夠清楚，而且開頭文字太多，因此我們刪減文字，並以色塊區隔各章節，讓頁面更容易閱讀。其次，開頭太難。為了讓更多人能使用平台，我們降低了開頭與結尾章節的難度，並加入動手實作任務，讓學習者透過實作來理解。","Such an online platform allows children to access science knowledge in a correct and fun way. by a Director of Student Affairs in Elementary":"這樣的線上平台，讓孩子們能以正確且有趣的方式接觸科學知識。 ——一位國小學務主任","The modules stand alone, so another team or teacher can take one module, adapt it to their own project, or add a module of their own.":"各模組都能獨立使用，因此其他團隊或教師可以選用其中一個模組、將它調整為適合自己的專題，或新增自己的模組。","Mushroom Body Lobes / MBON: output (validation and handover)":"蘑菇體葉部／蘑菇體輸出神經元（MBON）：輸出（驗證與交接）","Kenyon cell axons run through the mushroom body lobes, where mushroom body output neurons (MBONs) read the learned pattern and convert it into an actual decision — approach or avoid. It's the output stage — the subject of Module 5 (Decide) of our online Learning Lab — and biologically, it's where internal learning becomes visible, external behavior.":"Kenyon 細胞的軸突穿過蘑菇體葉部，蘑菇體輸出神經元（MBON）在此讀取學到的模式，並將其轉化為實際決策——接近或避開。這是輸出階段——也是我們線上 Learning Lab 模組 5（決策）的主題——而在生物學上，這裡就是內在學習轉變為可見、外在行為的地方。","The projects here aren't about reach or depth — they're about what happens when our work gets read out to an outside expert audience and has to hold up: an industry conference, a peer iGEM team, and an academic lecture hall. It also holds the two ways our work leaves the room: a toolkit other teachers can run, and an exhibition of what participants made.":"這裡的計畫不以觸及範圍或學習深度為重點，而是關注當我們的工作呈現給外部專業受眾，並且必須經得起檢視時，會發生什麼事：產業研討會、同儕 iGEM 團隊，以及學術演講廳。這一部分也包含讓我們的工作走出現場的兩種方式：其他教師能夠使用的工具包，以及參與者創作的展覽。","1. SynBioBeta 2026 — Next-Gen BioLeaders & Poster Session":"1. SynBioBeta 2026——Next-Gen BioLeaders 與海報發表","Everything else in this section teaches people who came to us. SynBioBeta reverses the direction. It is where working synthetic biologists, founders and investors evaluate each other's work, and the Next-Gen BioLeaders program puts emerging leaders in the room with that community. For an education project, that was a chance to be the learner, and to test whether our story, \"a smell is a pattern, read by a fly-inspired circuit,\" can be understood by non-specialists in a few minutes at a poster.":"本章其他活動，都是向前來參與的人教學。SynBioBeta 則反轉了這個方向。這裡是在業界工作的合成生物學家、創業者與投資人彼此評估工作的場合，而 Next-Gen BioLeaders 計畫讓新興領導者有機會與這個社群同處一室。對一項教育計畫而言，這是成為學習者的機會，也能檢驗我們所述說的「氣味是一組模式，由受到果蠅啟發的電路讀取」這個故事，是否能讓非專業人士在海報前幾分鐘內理解。","At SynBioBeta 2026 (San Jose, May 4 to 7), as one of the Next-Gen BioLeaders, with our poster accepted and presented in the Expo Hall. The poster, \"Development of a Bionic Olfactory Edge Computing System Integrating Drosophila Neural Models and Live-Cell Sensor Arrays,\" fit the whole platform on one page for a mixed audience: why conventional electronic noses fall short, how the fly solves the problem, and why we use living cells.":"在 SynBioBeta 2026（聖荷西，5 月 4 至 7 日）中，我們作為 Next-Gen BioLeaders 的一員，海報獲得接受，並在展覽廳發表。這張題為「整合果蠅神經模型與活細胞感測器陣列的仿生嗅覺邊緣運算系統開發」的海報，將整個平台濃縮在一頁中，呈現給不同背景的受眾：傳統電子鼻為何有所不足、果蠅如何解決這個問題，以及我們為什麼使用活細胞。","The poster showed us where the explanation broke. A PhD student from UCLA, with a wet-lab background, told us he had not known how a live-cell sensor is actually built. That was the step we had explained least.":"海報讓我們看見說明在哪裡出現斷層。一位具備濕實驗背景的 UCLA 博士生告訴我們，他原先並不知道活細胞感測器實際上是如何建構的。那正是我們說明得最少的一個步驟。","The hardest question we were asked was whether our living-cell system can scale. Two more followed: how a medically positioned device would be regulated, and whether the hardware has enough margin. They came from people who evaluate companies, not student projects.":"我們被問到最困難的問題，是活細胞系統能否擴大規模。接著還有兩個問題：以醫療用途定位的裝置會如何受到監管，以及硬體是否有足夠的餘裕。這些問題來自評估企業的人，而非評估學生專題的人。","Our formal Human Practices work had not yet begun in May, so this was our first read on the project from outside the lab, and the questions landed on the wet lab, the model and the hardware. They changed our plan and led us to add consultations. The scale question led to state the concrete follow-up, such as a cartridge-lifetime test or a consultation on cell production. The regulatory question led us to add regulatory consultation and to move our first application from medical diagnostics to agriculture, where the path to market is more accessible.":"我們正式的 Human Practices 工作在 5 月尚未開始，因此，這是專題首次得到實驗室之外的檢視，而問題涵蓋了濕實驗、模型與硬體。這些問題改變了我們的計畫，也促使我們增加諮詢。規模化的問題促使我們說明具體的後續行動，例如匣體壽命測試或細胞生產諮詢。監管問題則促使我們增加法規諮詢，並將第一項應用從醫療診斷轉向市場進入途徑較為可行的農業領域。","The poster's wording changed with the plan. The April poster lists medical point-of-care testing, including non-invasive breath diagnostics, alongside agriculture and environmental monitoring; our current materials present AeroSense as an agricultural and food-safety screening platform.":"海報的措辭隨著計畫而改變。4 月的海報將包含非侵入式呼氣診斷在內的醫療即時照護檢測，與農業、環境監測並列；我們目前的資料則將 AeroSense 呈現為農業與食品安全篩檢平台。","2. Mini Jamboree (with International iGEM community)":"2. Mini Jamboree（與國際 iGEM 社群交流）","Most of our audiences so far were people who know little about our field. Other iGEM teams are the opposite: they know what a weak result looks like, and they run education projects of their own. A cross-border meeting with them gave us two things we could not get from our own audiences, expert criticism of our design and a look at how other teams teach.":"到目前為止，我們的大多數受眾都不太了解我們的領域。其他 iGEM 團隊則恰恰相反：他們知道薄弱的結果是什麼樣子，也各自執行教育計畫。與他們進行跨國交流，帶給我們兩項無法從原有受眾取得的收穫：對我們設計的專業批評，以及了解其他團隊如何教學的機會。","On October 8, 2026, iGEM TAU-Israel hosted an online Mini Jamboree. Eight teams from six countries took part: NCKU-Tainan and NTHU from Taiwan, CAU-China and AIS-China from China, CERNAL from Israel, Cell Forge from India, iGEM-UA Alicante from Spain, and UFRGS-Brazil. Each team presented for about fifteen minutes, so every team heard seven other projects and every project was heard by teams in different regions with different regulations, farming and school systems. Besides our project, we also shared the education work described on this page, so that our activities could be compared with theirs.":"2026 年 10 月 8 日，iGEM TAU-Israel 舉辦了一場線上 Mini Jamboree。來自六個國家的八支團隊參與：臺灣的 NCKU-Tainan 與 NTHU、中國的 CAU-China 與 AIS-China、以色列的 CERNAL、印度的 Cell Forge、西班牙的 iGEM-UA Alicante，以及 UFRGS-Brazil。每支團隊發表約十五分鐘，因此，每支團隊都聽到了另外七個專題，而每個專題也都讓來自不同地區、擁有不同法規、農業與學校制度的團隊聽見。除了專題本身，我們也分享了本頁所描述的教育工作，讓我們的活動能與他們的活動相互比較。","We received feedback on our model design from teams outside our own circle, and we exchanged education activities with them.":"我們收到來自原有圈子之外團隊對模型設計的回饋，也與他們交流了教育活動。","ADD: the main model comments, and what we changed or will test because of them.":"待補充：主要的模型意見，以及我們據此做了哪些改變，或將進行哪些測試。","ADD: one education idea from another team that we have used or plan to use.":"待補充：一項來自其他團隊、我們已採用或計畫採用的教育構想。","3. China Medical University Guest Lecture":"3. 中國醫藥大學客座演講","The circuit our classifier is built on comes from research co-published by our advisor, Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo, and Prof. Ching-Che Charng of China Medical University (Cheng et al., Science Advances, 2025). Prof. Charng invited us to bring that shared research back to his university, to an audience that could judge how we had used it.":"我們分類器所依據的神經迴路，來自指導教授羅中泉教授與中國醫藥大學張景哲教授共同發表的研究（Cheng 等人，Science Advances，2025）。張教授邀請我們將這項共同研究帶回他的學校，向能夠評估我們如何運用該研究的受眾分享。","On September 23, 2026, a member of our model team gave a research-sharing lecture on our electronic-nose work to more than thirty undergraduate and graduate students at China Medical University. The lecture followed one thread: why electronic noses drift and why recalibrating them is costly; how the insect olfactory system keeps its odor code stable; and how our spiking neural network borrows those ideas. We also presented the results that do not flatter the model: the 14 sensors in our test dataset behave like only three types, adding more features did not help once the data had been compressed, and accuracy fell to about 75% when odors were presented continuously. We taught the evidence together with its limits so that listeners could judge the method themselves.":"2026 年 9 月 23 日，我們模型組的一位成員，在中國醫藥大學向三十多位大學生與研究生，進行了關於電子鼻工作的研究分享演講。演講沿著一條主線展開：電子鼻為什麼會漂移，以及重新校正為何成本高昂；昆蟲嗅覺系統如何維持氣味編碼的穩定；以及我們的脈衝神經網路如何借鑑這些概念。我們也呈現了對模型並不有利的結果：測試資料集中的 14 個感測器，表現得如同只有三種類型；資料壓縮後，增加更多特徵並沒有幫助；而在連續呈現氣味時，準確率降至約 75%。我們將證據與其限制一併教給聽眾，讓他們能自行判斷這個方法。","Most of the audience's questions were about how the model processes an odor: how sensor readings become a pattern, and how that pattern becomes a decision. They showed us that this step needs a plainer explanation than we had given. We changed how we introduced the model in the olfactory neuroscience workshop that followed.":"聽眾的大多數問題，都與模型如何處理氣味有關：感測器讀值如何形成模式，以及這個模式如何轉化為決策。這些問題讓我們看見，相較於先前的說明，這個步驟需要更淺白的解釋。我們因此改變了在後續嗅覺神經科學工作坊中介紹模型的方式。","4. Art Exhibition":"4. 藝術展覽","We asked participants of the elementary school science camp, the olfactory neuroscience workshop and other activities to draw \"the electronic nose and the fruit fly as you imagine them,\" and we treat their drawings as a creative output of our education work. What a learner draws shows what they took away in their own terms, which a quiz cannot show. The drawings are displayed on our Art Gallery page":"我們邀請國小科學營、嗅覺神經科學工作坊與其他活動的參與者，畫出「你想像中的電子鼻與果蠅」，並將這些畫作視為教育工作的創意成果。學習者畫出的內容，以他們自己的方式呈現了他們帶走的收穫，而這是測驗無法呈現的。這些畫作展示於我們的 Art Gallery 頁面。","5. Teacher Toolkit & Education Guide — open resources":"5. 教師工具包與教育指南——開放資源","Teacher Toolkit. When we met the principal of the elementary school where we ran our science camp, he told us he liked the way we teach and asked for a way to keep using it, since we cannot visit every year. We packaged the camp into a teacher toolkit: the lesson slides, the Odor Pixel Suite game, and instructions for using the Learning Lab, so that a teacher can run the same session without us. The school welcomed the approach, and the toolkit is free for any teacher to download.":"教師工具包。當我們與舉辦科學營的國小校長見面時，他告訴我們，他喜歡我們的教學方式，也希望有一種方式能夠持續使用，因為我們無法每年都到訪。我們將營隊整理為教師工具包：課程投影片、Odor Pixel Suite 遊戲，以及 Learning Lab 使用說明，讓教師能在沒有我們在場的情況下，進行相同的課程。學校歡迎這個做法，而工具包也開放所有教師免費下載。","Teacher Toolkit - Google Drive":"教師工具包——Google Drive","Education Guide. The Education Guide is written for other teams, as a PDF on our Contribution page. It sets out the steps we followed: find out what your audience believes, choose one claim, match the format to the audience, measure the same way each time, and hand the work on, so that a team that has never met us can plan its own education work.":"教育指南。教育指南是為其他團隊撰寫的 PDF，放在我們的 Contribution 頁面。它列出我們遵循的步驟：了解受眾抱持哪些看法、選定一項主張、讓形式符合受眾、每次都以相同方式評量，以及將工作交接出去，讓從未與我們見過面的團隊，也能規劃自己的教育工作。","Closing":"結語","We started this track by testing an assumption instead of trusting it — and found that the honest, narrow answer (\"most people already know mold is dangerous; a few still trust heat or their nose to check it\") was more useful than the broad one we'd assumed going in. Every project on this page, from a three-game suite to an art exhibition, exists to close the loop on that one specific, testable claim — carried from first contact (Region 1), through structured learning (Region 2), to outside validation and handover (Region 3).":"我們以檢驗一項假設，而非直接相信它，作為這條路線的起點——並發現誠實且聚焦的答案（「大多數人已經知道黴菌很危險；少數人仍相信加熱或自己的鼻子能用來判斷」），比我們起初預設的籠統答案更有用。本頁的每項計畫，從三款遊戲構成的套組到藝術展覽，都為了針對這一項具體、可檢驗的主張完成回饋循環——從初次接觸（區域 1），經過有架構的學習（區域 2），到外部驗證與交接（區域 3）。","References":"參考資料","Try the decision questions":"試試決策問題","Archived survey data":"封存問卷資料","Teacher toolkit and guide":"教師工具包與指南","Source note awaiting completion":"原始記錄待補項目","SynBioBeta 2026 poster · PDF":"SynBioBeta 2026 海報 · PDF","Our formal Human Practices work had not yet begun in May, so this was our first read on the project from outside the lab, and the questions landed on the wet lab, the model and the hardware. They changed our plan and led us to add consultations.":"我們正式的 Human Practices 工作在 5 月尚未開始，因此，這是專題首次得到實驗室之外的檢視，而問題涵蓋了濕實驗、模型與硬體。這些問題改變了我們的計畫，也促使我們增加諮詢。","The scale question led to state the concrete follow-up, such as a cartridge-lifetime test or a consultation on cell production.":"規模化問題所引出的具體後續行動仍需寫明，例如匣體壽命測試或細胞生產諮詢。","The regulatory question led us to add regulatory consultation and to move our first application from medical diagnostics to agriculture, where the path to market is more accessible.":"監管問題則促使我們增加法規諮詢，並將第一項應用從醫療診斷轉向市場進入途徑較為可行的農業領域。","Module 01 · Discover — How do we smell?":"單元 01 · 探索 — 我們如何聞到氣味？","Build an odor fingerprint":"建立氣味指紋","What exactly is a smell?":"氣味究竟是什麼？","Parts Design: the four-well sensor box.":"Parts Design：四孔感測盒。","Model: The cell lit up. Now what?":"Model：細胞發光了，接下來呢？","The SynBioBeta 2026 poster session hall.":"SynBioBeta 2026 海報展示會場。","An AeroSense presenter with the project poster at SynBioBeta 2026.":"AeroSense 發表者與 SynBioBeta 2026 專題海報。","The Programmable Protein Era panel at SynBioBeta 2026.":"SynBioBeta 2026 的 Programmable Protein Era 論壇。","Introducing iGEM during the China Medical University guest lecture.":"在中國醫藥大學客座講座中介紹 iGEM。","Presenting the AeroSense system at China Medical University.":"在中國醫藥大學介紹 AeroSense 系統。","Discussing odor-sensing applications at China Medical University.":"在中國醫藥大學討論氣味感測的應用。","山崎國小科普營隊.pdf":"山崎國小科普營隊.pdf","workshop 261014.pdf":"workshop 261014.pdf","mini jamboree.pdf":"mini jamboree.pdf","China Medical University Guest Lecture_compressed.pdf":"China Medical University Guest Lecture_compressed.pdf","Shan-chi Elementary School":"山崎國小","is a rural school in Xinfeng Township, Hsinchu County. Bringing a hands-on science session to a school there is a small step toward the equal access to quality education that SDG 4 describes. The camp also lets us test our claim that the game can be understood by children, instead of assuming it.":"是位於新竹縣新豐鄉的一所鄉村學校。將動手實作的科學活動帶進當地學校，是朝向 SDG 4 所描述的平等取得優質教育機會邁出的一小步。這場營隊也讓我們能夠檢驗「兒童能理解這款遊戲」的主張，而非直接假設如此。","From curiosity to informed decisions":"從好奇到有依據的決策","Practise the decision":"練習做決策","Our early survey redirected teaching from general mold awareness to decisions about heat, smell and visible spoilage. We built activities in which learners choose, receive an explanation and apply the idea again. The redesign used 28 responses; the later reported total of 107 still lacks verified item-level counts.":"早期問卷讓教學從黴菌的一般知識，轉向加熱、氣味與可見腐敗的判斷。我們設計了讓學習者選擇、閱讀解釋並再次應用的活動。這次改版依據 28 份回覆；後續回報的 107 份尚缺經核對的逐題統計。","Start with familiar choices":"從熟悉的選擇出發","Survey findings shaped the lessons":"問卷發現引導教學","Two collection stages":"兩階段問卷","Sample limitations":"樣本限制","Three browser games make odor patterns tangible through recognition, navigation and mixture decoding. These simplified models invite learners to test their intuition; formal learning evaluation is pending.":"三款瀏覽器遊戲透過辨識、導航與混合氣味解碼，讓氣味模式變得具體。學習者可在簡化模型中檢驗直覺；正式學習成效仍待評估。","Science in a social feed":"社群裡的科學","Instagram introduces the project through technical carousels, sustainability questions and short explanations. Each format connects one scientific idea to a familiar decision.":"Instagram 透過技術輪播、永續提問與簡短說明介紹專題，每種形式都將一個科學概念連結到熟悉的決策。","Connect the concepts":"串起核心概念","Learn through dialogue":"透過對話學習","Industry audiences, neuroscience students and other iGEM teams challenged different parts of our explanation. These exchanges helped us refine the story; they were not controlled learning trials.":"產業聽眾、神經科學學生與其他 iGEM 隊伍，分別挑戰了說明中的不同環節。交流協助我們修正敘事，但並非受控的學習成效試驗。","SynBioBeta exchange":"SynBioBeta 交流","Biology before engineering":"從生物原理理解工程","Learning across teams":"跨隊伍交流","Resources others can reuse":"可供他人再用的資源","Evaluate learning":"評估學習成效","Current evidence":"現有證據","Paired learning-gain evaluation is pending.":"配對學習成效評估尚待完成。","Reach measures exposure; learning requires assessment.":"觸及呈現接觸程度；學習成效需要評量。","Two assessment pathways":"兩條評量路徑","Each node identifies the delivered activity and its evaluation status.":"每個節點標明已提供的活動及其評估狀態。","Comparability and transfer":"可比性與知識遷移","Shared assessment items":"共用評量題目","What changed in our teaching":"教學如何改變","The record below links each piece of evidence to a teaching decision.":"以下紀錄將每項證據連結到具體教學決策。","Teach with AeroSense":"用 AeroSense 教學","Use the lessons, games and evaluation protocol in your own setting.":"將課程、遊戲及評估程序運用於自己的教學情境。","The game build, protocols and question bank are included in this wiki. The packaged teacher toolkit is still in preparation.":"本 wiki 已收錄遊戲、程序與題庫；整套教師工具包仍在準備中。","Evaluation limits":"評估限制","The resources are available; their effect on learning still requires a documented evaluation.":"教學資源已可使用，學習效果仍需有紀錄的評估。","Next: evaluate with learners":"下一步：與學習者共同評估","Our 28-response survey redirected teaching from general mold awareness to decisions about heat, smell and visible spoilage. Learners make a choice, examine the reasoning and apply the idea again.":"28 份問卷回覆使教學從一般黴菌認知，轉向加熱、氣味與可見腐敗的判斷。學習者先做選擇、檢視推理，再應用概念。","Active learning informed our approach. Freeman and colleagues synthesized 225 undergraduate STEM studies and reported an average 0.47-standard-deviation examination improvement. Wouters and colleagues found benefits of serious games for learning and retention.":"主動學習研究提供設計依據。Freeman 等人彙整 225 項大學 STEM 研究，報告考試表現平均提升 0.47 個標準差；Wouters 等人則發現嚴肅遊戲有助於學習與保留。","Choose an answer, read the reasoning and reconsider your decision. Choices remain in this browser tab.":"選擇答案、閱讀推理，再檢視自己的判斷。選擇保留在此瀏覽器分頁中。","The 23 August 2026 record contains 28 responses. Most respondents rejected all three claims, so we focused teaching on applying those ideas to food decisions.":"2026 年 8 月 23 日的記錄含 28 份回覆。多數受訪者否定三項說法，因此教學聚焦於如何把概念運用在食物判斷上。","The table reports aggregate counts from a convenience sample and guided curriculum design. Percentages use the stated denominators.":"表格呈現便利樣本的彙整計數，用於課程設計；百分比依列出的分母計算。","Three browser games teach odor patterns through recognition, navigation and mixture decoding.":"三款瀏覽器遊戲透過辨識、導航與混合物解碼，介紹氣味模式。","The first carousel follows an odor signal through the receptor, calcium entry and fluorescent reporter. The two published graphics introduce the receptor and reporter designs.":"第一組輪播圖沿著受體、鈣離子流入與螢光報導蛋白追蹤氣味訊號。兩張已發布圖解介紹受體與報導蛋白設計。","Each module includes a short assessment and personal feedback stored in the learner’s browser.":"每個模組包含簡短評量，個人回饋儲存在學習者的瀏覽器。","Industry audiences, neuroscience students and other iGEM teams helped us refine how we explain the project.":"業界觀眾、神經科學學生與其他 iGEM 隊伍協助我們改進專案說明。","The Learning Lab, browser games and educator protocol are available for reuse below.":"以下提供可重用的 Learning Lab、瀏覽器遊戲及教育者操作方法。","Use the same anonymous session and instrument for paired pre/post comparisons. Analyze food-safety decisions and olfactory-coding scores separately.":"前後測配對須使用同一匿名工作階段及評量工具；食安判斷與嗅覺編碼分數分開分析。","The curriculum uses two assessment chains: food-safety decisions and olfactory literacy. Shared item IDs connect equivalent questions within each chain.":"課程分為食安判斷與嗅覺素養兩條評量路徑；同一路徑內，以共用題目編號連結等同問題。","Module 2 belongs to Chain A; Modules 1, 3, 4 and 5 belong to Chain B.":"模組 2 屬於路徑 A；模組 1、3、4、5 屬於路徑 B。","Optional study mode pairs pre/post items and a transfer question, then exports anonymous JSON or CSV locally. The archived QC Shift G2 items apply to QC Shift; the current Maze has different learning objectives.":"選用研究模式可配對前後測與遷移題，並在本機匯出匿名 JSON 或 CSV。封存的 QC Shift G2 題目適用於 QC Shift；目前的迷宮遊戲有不同學習目標。","Educators can reproduce the optional evaluation workflow below.":"教育者可依下列步驟重現選用的評量流程。","Report paired-response counts and missing responses.":"報告配對回覆數與缺失回覆。","The 28-response survey found 27/28 rejected the mold-removal claim, 24/28 the heating claim and 23/28 the look-and-smell claim. We used those decisions to focus Module 2 and reuse the same item IDs.":"28 份回覆中，27/28 否定去除黴菌即可安全食用、24/28 否定加熱即可去除風險、23/28 否定外觀與氣味正常即安全。我們據此聚焦模組 2，並沿用相同題目編號。","An internal review identified a gap between odor-pattern games and the complete sensing system. We built the five-module Learning Lab to connect biology, engineering, computation and decisions.":"內部檢視發現，氣味模式遊戲尚未涵蓋完整感測系統。我們建立五模組 Learning Lab，串起生物、工程、運算與決策。","We revised Module 5 around the action following a screening result: monitor, retest or escalate to confirmation.":"我們將模組 5 聚焦於篩檢結果之後的行動：監測、複測或進行確認檢測。","The diagnostic record contains 28 responses and three aggregate item counts.":"診斷性問卷記錄含 28 份回覆及三項彙整計數。","Shared item IDs connect equivalent questions across the survey and Module 2.":"共用題目編號連結問卷與模組 2 的等同問題。","Select an activity to inspect its teaching method and reusable materials.":"選擇活動，查看教學方法與可重用教材。","Facilitator guide":"帶領者指南","Stable item IDs support traceable scoring.":"固定題目編號支援可追溯計分。","Discussion prompts are available within the Learning Lab.":"討論提示位於 Learning Lab 中。","Scores and reflections stay in the visitor’s browser.":"分數與反思保留在使用者的瀏覽器中。","Learning goals":"學習目標","You disagreed. Correct. The explanation below shows why.":"你選擇不同意，答對了。下方說明解釋原因。","You agreed. Reconsider this claim using the explanation below.":"你選擇同意。請閱讀下方說明，再想一想這個說法。","Why we teach":"為什麼教學","The brain-map journey":"腦神經圖譜之旅","Structured learning":"系統化學習","Exchange":"交流","Evidence and resources":"證據與資源"});
